\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Under Pressure Early, But Trading Stable \b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2000\par 03:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained under pressure early Friday as the prospects for tighter U.S. monetary policy underpinned the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the bias toward the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in global markets probably will be retained at least through next week's Federal Open Market Committee meeting, at which policy makers are expected to raise short-term interest rates by a half percentage point. \par \par \uc2  However, trading in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was relatively stable after a session Thursday that saw heavy volatility and rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah hovered around the 8,400 rupiah to the dollar level as poor investor sentiment and negative comments Thursday by the country's Senior Economics Minister Kwik Kian Gie weighed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0110 GMT (9:10 p.m. EDT Thursday), the dollar was quoted at IDR8,400, up slightly from IDR8,375 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar edged up after hitting a 13-month low a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7246, down from S$1.7265 late Thursday. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had risen to S$1.7351 Thursday before the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  was reported to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's behalf. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the continuing preference for U.S. dollars should keep the pair in a trading range of S$1.7250-$1.7290 Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht resumed its downward slide after being propped up a day earlier by technical factors. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  got a boost Thursday when foreign banks that bet on a decline in the baht were forced to pull back due to the rising cost of funding their long-dollar positions through offshore swaps. \par \par \uc2  But general sentiment toward the baht remained negative because of the expected U.S. rate hike and concern over the pace of debt restructuring in Thailand, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Early Friday, the dollar was quoted at 38.955 baht, up from THB38.815 late Thursday. Profit-taking is expected to cap the dollar's gains at THB39.000, with support at THB38.800, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit a 19-month high against the peso. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at PHP41.450, up from Thursday's close of PHP41.430. Further gains could be capped by the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers attribute the peso's weakness to the ongoing hostage crisis in the southern Philippines and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plan to keep key policy rates unchanged, despite the expected hike in U.S. rates. \par \par \uc2  Against the South Korean won, the dollar was quoted at 1,111.60 won, up from KRW1,109.10 at Wednesday's close. Markets in Seoul were closed Thursday for a holiday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expected the pair to trade between KRW1,109-KRW1,112 Friday. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar rose slightly as the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help erase some of Thursday's losses. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was quoted at NT$30.720, down from NT$30.752 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Yonan Jr.; 65 421-4859; alan.yonan@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5c02c2m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
