\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Browbeaten by dlr, c.banks jump in. \b0\par\par\uc2 984 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2000\par 10:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 11 (Reuters) - Hefty losses in regional \par \par \uc2  stocks and the prospect of higher U.S. rates put Asian regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the defensive late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      The fall was more pronounced in the rupiah and the baht \par \par \uc2  which hit their 2000 lows as flustered importers and corporate \par \par \uc2  players scurried to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2      Central banks in Indonesia, \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Thailand were \par \par \uc2  heard \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prop up their sliding \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but no official confirmation was available. \par \par \uc2      "Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales were broad-based. There's talk \par \par \uc2  that central banks were in the market today - Singapore, \par \par \uc2  Indonesia and Thailand," said Philip Wee, treasury economist at \par \par \uc2  Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      "The dollar offers were mostly done through offshore banks. \par \par \uc2  But there's no confirmation on this," he said. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would retain their weak tone \par \par \uc2  in the near-term against a backdrop of continued dollar \par \par \uc2  strength. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar briefly rose above the 110 yen\tab   barrier as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a sharp fall in Tokyo shares overshadowed confidence in Japan's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The benchmark Nikkei\tab    closed 4.63 percent off on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday, ending below 17,000 points for the first time since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par September 27, 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A stream of dollar bids from offshore and corporate players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sent the rupiah reeling to 8,420 -- its lowest level since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par September 29.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Although talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and sporadic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar profit-taking lifted the unit from its day low, market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment remained glum.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said any rebound could be temporary as corporate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar demand remained high and exporters were opting to park\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par their dollar receivables offshore amid political and economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par uncertainties.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht struggled to stand above the key 39.00 level where\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was rumoured to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said it was likely to slip back below the level\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par again soon due to sustained dollar demand from both offshore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and corporate players.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  declares that it had indeed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and that it hates to see the baht below 39, then market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par participants might perhaps hold their baht sales for a while,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said a dealer at a European bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "But I don't think sellers would be deterred much by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market talk," she said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar staged a mild rebound amid market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rumours that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to defend it after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it fell to 13-month lows against the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore (MAS) was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par spotted selling dollars fairly aggressively from the 1.7350\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level downwards, pushing the Sing dollar back to the firm side\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 1.73.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was also talk that the MAS had drained liquidity in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local money markets, pushing short-term interbank rates to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par their highest since the last quarter of 1998 on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par An MAS spokeswoman said the bank does not comment on its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par actions in the market. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has said in the past\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that it \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to smooth sharp moves in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the exchange rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso was at the lower end of its intra-day range,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offering few buying incentives as investors opted to wait for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the expected increase in U.S. interest rates next week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The unresolved armed conflict in the southern Mindanao region\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par also weighed on sentiment, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the macro front, the country's gross international\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reserves were $15.8 billion at the end of April, down from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $15.99 billion the previous month, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar took its cue from the weaker yen and a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par near 2.5 percent drop on the stock market, which pushed the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par benchmark TAIEX to its lowest close in 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said worries about the scale and impact of the next\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fed rate hike and hefty overnight losses on the Nasdaq\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were depressing Taipei markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar's plight was worsened by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's failure to defend the T$30.72 level, where it has been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seen recently, though dealers said the bank was in the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par intermittently over the course of the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been in the market of late and dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said its moves were aimed at eliminating market expectations of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a depreciation of the Taiwan dollar amid political\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par uncertainties.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won was quoted lower in thin offshore trade,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with local markets closed for Buddha's birthday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Finance Minister Lee Hun-Jai said Korea's GDP this year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would probably exceed an originally forecast six percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He also said inflation this year would be within the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par originally estimated three percent, while a strong export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par performance would yield a continued trade surplus.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Over the medium term, South Korea's GDP would be around six\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent and inflation below three percent, he added, without\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par specifying the time period.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0843 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     109.86\tab  109.40\tab    -0.42\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7262\tab  1.7297\tab    +0.20\par  Taiwan dlr    30.752\tab  30.697\tab    -0.18\par  Korean won   1112.50\tab 1109.00\tab    -0.31\par  Baht\tab      38.87\tab   38.89\tab    +0.05\par  Peso\tab      41.38\tab   41.37\tab    -0.02\par  Rupiah\tab  8380.00\tab 8190.00\tab    -2.27\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.86\tab  102.21\tab    -6.96\par  Sing dlr\