\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Late; Panic Selling Hurts Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2  By Alan Yonan Jr. \par \uc2 806 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2000\par 11:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah was driven sharply lower by panic selling Thursday, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prevent their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from being swept along, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah had been pressured all week by concerns over Indonesia's political and economic outlook, a softer yen, and prospects for higher U.S. interest rates. But it was dealt another blow Thursday by shocking comments from the country's top economic minister questioning the wisdom of investing in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia faces too much instability and social unrest to appeal to investors, Senior Economics Minister Kwik Kian Gie said in an interview with Dow Jones Newswires. \par \par \uc2  "I never talk about foreign investment and things like that because I'm realistic enough; if I were a foreign investor, I wouldn't come to Indonesia," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The law enforcement is not there. But not only that, the whole thing is so confusing. How can you come here?," he asked. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah reacted negatively, falling to nearly a seven-month low against the dollar. The dollar touched 8,430 rupiah in intraday trading, the strongest it has been against the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since hitting IDR8,492 on Oct. 14, 1999. \par \par \uc2  Near the end of Asian trading, the dollar was quoted at IDR8,375, up from IDR8,203 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "Kwik is apparently unhappy with President Wahid's decision to appoint two advisors to oversee the activities in his ministry," said Philip Wee, treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "It's difficult to see any respite for the (rupiah), especially after it broke through key resistance at 8,200. Neighboring \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are in for a rough ride as well," Wee said. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso, New Taiwan dollar, Singapore dollar and Thai baht also traded lower for most of the day before the latter two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered somewhat in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  In the case of the Singapore dollar, dealers said the rebound was at least partially driven by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, which entered the market late in the afternoon to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide. \par \par \uc2  The MAS has a policy of not commenting on its monetary actions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the MAS' action was driven more by its desire to show the market that it has control over its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  than any significant concern about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value relative to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has risen significantly against the euro, yen and other world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on expectations that Federal Reserve policy makers will raise short-term interest rates by a half a percentage point next week. \par \par \uc2  Because the dollar strength is broad-based, and not aimed specifically at the Singapore dollar, it is of less concern to the MAS, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "They (MAS) were just trying to send a message to the market," a dealer at a foreign bank said. "There was so much panic in the market today...they just wanted to prevent undue volatility," he said. \par \par \uc2  The MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the dollar hit a 13-month high of S$1.7351, dealers at three different foreign banks said. The MAS sold dollars all the way down to the $1.7250 level, they said. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asian trading, the dollar was quoted at S$1.7265, down from S$1.7301 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht spent most of the day battling poor sentiment spurred by the expected U.S. rate hike, stock market outflows and concerns over the pace of debt restructuring in Thailand. \par \par \uc2  At its high point, the dollar broke through a key THB39.00 resistance level for the first time since November 1999. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar reversed course in the afternoon after offshore players, who held long dollar positions through swap contracts, took profit on the dollar's rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Late in the session the dollar was quoted at 38.815 baht, down from THB38.915 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso closed lower on prospects for a widening interest rate differential with the U.S., as well a rebel uprising in the southern part of the country. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 41.430 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, up from Wednesday's close at PHP41.370. Earlier in the session, the dollar rose to a 19-month high of PHP41.440. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar ended lower Thursday following a 2.5% drop in the local stock market index. Foreign institutional investors, who helped boost the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months, sold a net NT$3.09 billion worth of Taiwan shares Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar closed at NT$30.752, compared with it's previous close at NT$30.697. \par \par \uc2  Markets in South Korea were closed for a holiday. \par \par \uc2  (Grainne McCarthy in Jakarta contributed to this article.) \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5b02dge\par }\page {\par\fs20