\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Easier, defenseless against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2000\par 11:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 10 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  eased further late on Wednesday as investors extended a flight \par \par \uc2  to the dollar, betting on an aggressive U.S. interest rate hike \par \par \uc2  next week. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro\tab   stabilised near earlier one-week highs\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around $0.91 after a newspaper reported the ECB was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "intensively considering" switching to variable rate tenders\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from the present fixed-rate regime.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen\tab   remained pressured by NTT Docomo's\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par purchase of a 15 percent stake in Dutch firm KPN Mobile\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also dimmed by further evidence of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign retreat from Japanese equities, showing overseas\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors were net sellers in April for the first time since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par September 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab    -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won bucked the regional downtrend as dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows from foreign stock funds and exporter sales outweighed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Seoul said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market saw inflows of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about $150 million from foreign investors' recent stock buying.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the won's upside was capped by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  concerns\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of a market holiday on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar was easier, as souring regional sentiment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par drove investors towards the greenback.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the market was cautiously eyeing 1.7310 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollar, a level where the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was expected to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Further support was seen at 1.7400 in the near term, while\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resistance was pegged at 1.7260.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht fell to a low of 38.98 -- its lowest level since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par December 7 -- on active dollar demand from offshore players and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local companies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Although dollar profit taking and offers prompted by tight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht liquidity offshore slowed its fall, they were not enough\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to lift the unit, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht was hit by local corporate players buying dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to refinance foreign debts and expectations that more people\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would act in that fashion, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Talk that Morgan Stanley Capital International, which is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closely tracked by fund managers, was expected to lower\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand's weighting to about 3.2 percent from 4.2 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par currently also dampened sentiment, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     One U.S. bank in Singapore was heard buying dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par aggressively on behalf of investment funds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah slid through the key 8,200 support on a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par combination of U.S. rate fears and concerns over the country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par political stability and economic progress.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Exporters who are earning U.S. dollar receivables\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overwhelmingly prefer to keep those earnings in U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deposits offshore," said David Simmonds, regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strategist at Citibank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In addition, importers are scrambling to buy dollars to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cover import liabilities early on expectations that those\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars will get expensive going forward," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar was a touch softer in slow trade as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par persistent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eroded some losses\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resulting from the yen's weakness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The key TAIEX\tab    market closed lower on Wednesday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mirroring Wall Street's fall on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market was also eyeing the inauguration of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par President-elect Chen Shui-bian on May 20.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso came off quite a bit on weaker regionals, expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. rate hikes and political concerns.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bid and offer rates of Philippine Treasury bills, which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par normally reflect market rate expectations, jumped by five to 15\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par basis points in the secondary market on Wednesday due to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par same factors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the downside could be limited as traders expected the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the unit drops below 41.40.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0933 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     109.40\tab  109.04\tab    -0.33\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7297\tab  1.7244\tab    -0.31\par  Taiwan dlr    30.697\tab  30.690\tab    -0.02\par  Korean won   1109.00\tab 1109.20\tab    +0.02\par  Baht\tab      38.89\tab   38.54\tab    -0.90\par  Peso\tab      41.37\tab   41.28\tab    -0.22\par  Rupiah\tab  8190.00\tab 8075.00\tab    -1.40\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7997\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.40\tab  102.21\tab    -6.57\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7297\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.80\par  Taiwan dlr    30.697\tab  31.380\tab    +2.22\par  Korean won   1109.0