\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Strong dollar smothers regionals. \b0\par\par\uc2 941 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2000\par 04:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 10 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  were easier on Wednesday, as investor appetite for dollars \par \par \uc2  showed no signs of letting up amid expectations of an \par \par \uc2  aggressive Fed rate hike next week. \par \par \uc2      The rupiah fell through 8,100 to the dollar to its weakest \par \par \uc2  levels since mid-October in early morning trade, hit by fresh \par \par \uc2  offshore dollar buying on concerns over the country's political \par \par \uc2  stability and economic progress. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar kept its firm stance against the yen\tab  ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par helped by commercial demand and buying interest from Japanese\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trust banks looking to unwind earlier hedge positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The ailing euro\tab   held most gains against the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in morning trade after hitting a high of 90.80 cents overnight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on wariness of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by European authorities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro got a boost overnight when French Finance Minister\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Laurent Fabius reminded markets that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was a weapon at Europe's disposal.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But underlying bearish sentiment for the euro remained, as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par doubts about actual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  still lingered.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah looked set to test the psychological 8,200\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support on a combination of U.S. rate fears and concerns over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the country's political stability and economic progress.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The rupiah is most likely to maintain its weak tone for a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par while," said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Uncertainties about the peaking of U.S. interest rates in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par terms of timing and magnitude and lack of foreign interest in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Indonesia) should limit investment inflows into the country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par And that is bearish for the rupiah," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said its upside would be capped at 8,050-8,100\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par where active bargain hunting on the dollar was expected. THAI\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht dipped through a key support of 38.60 on strong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar demand from local firms seeking to repay or refinance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign debts in the face of rising international interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said baht bids against the Singapore dollar had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slowed the fall, but would not be sufficient to stop it. Some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reckoned the unit could test the next support of 38.80 later on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts believe the widening differential between local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the U.S. interest rates suggests significant capital\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outflows will continue for the rest of this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Thailand's private foreign debt was estimated at around $36\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion in February.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso tracked the regionals lower in light trade, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers reckoned the downside should be limited by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was likely to be wedged in a narrow range and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading would remain light until the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  releases its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par grip on the market, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab    -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won started the day weaker against the dollar as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players looked to buy the U.S. unit as it strengthened against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Dollar sentiment is strong this morning as Asian\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , including the yen, appeared weaker versus the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unit," said a foreign bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Another dealer said the overhang and the bearish sentiment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were pushing the regionals lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Seoul dealers said they expected dollar/won to move in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tight range between 1,109.5 and 1,110.5 for the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar was dragged down by other regionals\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the yen though dealers were cautious of possible\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (MAS).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "People are expecting the MAS to come in to prop up the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing," said one dealer at a European bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But he saw no reason for the MAS to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at this level\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were generally weak. He expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Sing dollar to test the downside of 1.74 next week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders expected a narrow range of 1.7260-1.7310 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday with a focus on moves in the yen and the embattled\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Lacking fresh incentives, the Taiwan dollar remained\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trapped in a range with markets warily eyeing the inauguration\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of President-elect Chen Shui-bian on May 20.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Chen, a member of the pro-independence DPP (Democratic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Progressive Party), said on Tuesday he would neither provoke\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the island's giant communist neighbour nor give in too much.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In Beijing, Tang Shubei, a top Chinese negotiator with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan, pressed Chen to embrace the mainland's cherished "one\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China" principle. Tang warned that Taiwan's new administration\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would "create extremely grave new problems" if it failed to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par adhere to the "one China" policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Standard and Poor's MMS said in a report the Taiwan dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was poised to test the downside but was not likely to fall\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par beyond 30.80 even if any sudden cross-strait tension erupted.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0210 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     109.25\tab  109.04\tab    -0.19\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7282\tab  1.7244\tab    -0.22\par  Taiwan dlr    30.710\tab  30.690\tab    -0.07\par  Korean won   1109.40\tab 1109.20\tab    -0.02\par  Baht\tab      38.68\tab   38.54\tab    -0.36\par  Peso\tab      41.36\tab   41.28\tab    -0.19\par  Rupiah\tab  8150.00\tab 8075.00\tab    -0.92\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7997\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.25\tab  102.21\tab    -6.44\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7282\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.71\par  Taiwan dlr    30.710\tab  31.380\tab    +2.18\par  Korean won   1109.40\tab 1135.00\tab    +2.31\par  Baht\tab      38.68\tab   37.45\tab    -3.18\par  Peso\tab      41.36\tab   40.20\tab    -2.80\par  Rupiah\tab  8150.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -14.42\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7997\tab  3.7997\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Desk (65) 870-3087\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par email:asia.\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 @reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \