\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Easier, eyeing stock markets. \b0\par\par\uc2 988 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2000\par 04:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 9 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  mostly easier in early trade on Monday, with players eyeing \par \par \uc2  moves in local stock markets following losses in the Nasdaq \par \par \uc2  overnight. \par \par \uc2      Dollar demand from corporate players rushing to repay \par \par \uc2  foreign debts ahead of the Federal Reserve's May 16 meeting. \par \par \uc2  The vast majority in the market expect an aggressive \par \par \uc2  tightening. \par \par \uc2      Analysts believe some countries will opt to keep their \par \par \uc2  interest rates steady after any Fed's rates hike, but at the \par \par \uc2  expense of weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the yen\tab     quickly regained some ground against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar after being pressured by early morning by losses in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nikkei.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar dipped below 109 yen, weighed by profit-taking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and sporadic sales by exporters after failing to break above\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resistance at 109.20-30 earlier.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro stayed around previous fragile levels against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar\tab     and the yen\tab \tab  after euro-zone finance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ministers stopped short of threatening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The ministers issued a statement on Monday expressing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "common concern" about the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro looked under pressure against the yen, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exporters eagerly looking for chances to sell euros on rallies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won is expected to be driven by the equity markets. It\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was a tad weaker in early trade as foreign investors turned net\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sellers of local stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors, who bought a net 191.9 billion won worth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of shares on the Korea Stock Exchange on Monday, were net\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sellers of 8.3 billion won in morning trade by 0105 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Support is pegged around 1107 which represents the lows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tested in late April. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected around 1111\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which are the recent highs.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar edged lower from late Asian trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par levels while the market lacked strong incentives.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders said the dollar's moves would be key to determine\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the direction for the Sing but also kept an eye on sales from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The unit is expected to trade between 1.7180 and 1.7300 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht got some reprieve after offshore players unloaded\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars to ease tight baht liquidity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     As a result, one-month offshore swap premium dipped to 8/11\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par satangs per dollar from 12/15 early on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But any upside for the baht is seen limited, with pressure\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from strong local corporate dollar demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Companies rushed to buy the U.S. unit to repay foreign debts\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for fears that the looming U.S. rates hike could further put\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the defensive, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah lost further ground after it dipped below 8,000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late Monday as companies bought dollars to pay back debt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers expected the rupiah to retain its weak tone to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade between 7,900 and 8,100 on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said in the near term, focus had shifted from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par political uncertainty and the IMF's delayed loan to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar's general strength against regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Economics Minister Kwik Kian Gie said on Monday Jakarta's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par next letter of intent with the IMF could be signed on June 1 or\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2, paving the way for the release of the $400 million loan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso hovered sideways in early Asian trading, heading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its way into a third steady session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the tone was bearish as in other regionals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "There's still buying interest in dollar/peso from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Americans. In general, the dollar is strong against regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and equity sentiment is weak," said one European\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the market cautioned \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which put a floor on the peso at 41.30. Dealers forcast a range\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 41.25-41.30 for Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The near-term direction of the Taiwan dollar is likely to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be hinged on the performance of the local stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the unit is seen moving in a narrow range with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a downward bias in sluggish trade as sentiment weighed by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par losses in the Nasdaq overnight and linging cross-strait\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par concerns.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0144 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     108.73\tab  108.75\tab    +0.02\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7245\tab  1.7232\tab    -0.08\par  Taiwan dlr    30.692\tab  30.681\tab    -0.04\par  Korean won   1109.70\tab 1109.50\tab    -0.02\par  Baht\tab      38.40\tab   38.45\tab    +0.13\par  Peso\tab      41.26\tab   41.24\tab    -0.0