\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Ends Lower;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Threat Limits Loss \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2000\par 11:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar ended lower Tuesday against the U.S. dollar as the U.S. unit continued to gain ground on world markets, but the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited the local dollar's losses. \par \par \uc2  Around 0920 GMT (5:20 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7242, up slightly from S$1.7237 late Monday but down from an intraday peak of S$1.7261. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was at Y109.13, up from Y108.89 late Monday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  With U.S. dollar rising above Y109, many market participants had expected the Singapore dollar to be weaker. But the danger of action by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited its losses, they said. \par \par \uc2  Because the MAS has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell U.S. dollars above the level of S$1.7200 in the past, there was a reluctance to bid the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  much higher, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is quite cautious around this level," said a trader at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  One trader said the MAS, acting through local banks, was offering to sell the U.S. dollar at the level of S$1.7260, although that couldn't be confirmed. The MAS didn't actually buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the trader said. \par \par \uc2  Despite the MAS offers, the U.S. dollar may yet move up against its Singapore counterpart if it continues to gain against the euro, yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think MAS is going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  too aggressively yet," a dealer said. "They just want to avoid panic selling of Singapore dollar assets." \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered unchanged at 3.000%, while the three-month rate was offered at 3.0625%, up from 3.000%. \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5902aho\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
