\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Heartened by dollar's retreat. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,005 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2000\par 11:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 5 (Reuters) - Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  generally well-supported in late trade on Friday after the \par \par \uc2  dollar gave up some of its recent broad-based gains. \par \par \uc2      Most banks and businesses managed to shield themselves from \par \par \uc2  the "Love Bug" computer virus which wreaked havoc in e-mail \par \par \uc2  systems worldwide, dealer said. \par \par \uc2      The U.S. unit's retreat triggered short covering of local \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen\tab     advanced further against the dollar on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand from European names. A break through 107.50 is expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to trigger heavy stop-loss sales in dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro extended losses against the yen\tab \tab  amid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par growing optimism about the Japanese economic recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It held steady against the dollar, drawing little support\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from comments from European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Wim\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Duisenberg that the ECB monitors the euro exchange rate "very\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closely."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese former vice minister Eisuke Sakakibara said on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday that the European Union needed to take action to stop\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the euro's slide.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "They need to sort of accompany their words with action -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par what kind of action is up to them," Sakakibara told Reuters on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the sidelines of an Asian Development Bank meeting in Thailand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht remained weak in light trade as the onshore market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was closed for the Coronation Day holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Although the dollar remained generally well-bid against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thai unit, the upside is seen technically limited.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Technical analysts said the dollar/baht has bounced off a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par major Fibonacci retracement level that could provide it with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quite stiff upside resistance.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The 38.2 percent Fibonacci retracement of the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par downmove from the September 1999 high of 41.70 to the January\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2000 low of 36.71 stands at 38.62 baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar is likely to struggle to break this level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah lost ground in late Asian trading after testing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par immediate resistance at 7,940 earlier.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Local speculators and European offshore players joined\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par state banks in selling dollars in morning trade but a stream of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate dollar demand was seen capping the rupiah's upside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     One U.S. bank dealer said dollar/rupiah could venture into\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par new territory of 7,700 to 7,800 if the IMF agreed to disburse\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the delayed $400 million loan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank Indonesia Governor Syahril Sabirin said on Friday a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. rate hike would slow the bank's policy of bringing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rate down, but would not have a severe impact.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won was traded only offshore with thin volume due to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Children's Day holiday in Korea.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It remained paralysed around 1111 in late Asian trading,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hardly moving from Friday's earlier levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market expected little movement next week but kept a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close eye on the yen as the Korea and Japan markets both resume\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "If dollar/yen traded above 107, I think 1,110 would be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par good support," a dealer in Singapore said, adding that a dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par move to the 106 yen level would prompt a range of 1,090 to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,105 won.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A senior advisor to the Finance Minister said on Friday he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par did not expect Korea to raise rates in the near future in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wake of slowing economic growth and weak inflationary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressures.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar reversed course to slide in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par afternoon on concerns of dollar-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts said the Sing dollar would remain bearish,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possibly testing a previous day low of 1.7240.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Sources said on Friday Singapore Telecommunications Ltd\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (SingTel)  was seeking to enlist a Chinese partner as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it considered relaunching its bid for Cable & Wireless HKT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts said the move would serve to keep pressure on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SingTel was down S$0.03 at S$2.34 at 0855 GMT while Cable &\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wireless HKT was down HK$0.10 at HK$18.10.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was left out of the regional party on Friday as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors found few incentives to hold on to the unit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The policy-setting Philippine Monetary Board decided on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday to keep overnight rates steady following the release of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par milder-than-expected April inflation data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It also hinted that it might keep rates unchanged at next\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week's meeting. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hiked overnight rates by 25\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par basis points on May 2 to prop up the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Consumer prices rose 3.7 percent in the 12 months to April\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after rising 3.3 percent in March. A Reuters poll of 10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economists had forecast annual April inflation at 4.01 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar took heart from the yen's rebound against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar and robust gains in the local stock market which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closed 3.24 percent higher at 8,698.53.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Taipei said heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday's session kept trading interest light.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Chartists saw the immediate resistance for the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/Taiwan dollar at 30.72 and the next resistance at 30.80.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0904 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     107.53\tab  108.62\tab    +1.01\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7208\tab  1.7225\tab    +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr    30.648\tab  30.689\tab    +0.13\par  Korean won   1111.00\tab 1111.00\tab    +0.00\par  Baht\tab      38.52\tab   38.51\tab    -0.03\par  Peso\tab      41.25\tab   41.09\tab    -0.39\par  Rupiah\tab  7970.00\tab 7985.00\tab    +0.19\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     107.53\tab  102.21\tab    -4.95\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7208\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.30\par  Taiwan dlr    30.648\tab  31.380\tab    +2.39\par  Korean won   1111.00\tab 1135.00\tab    +2.16\par  Baht\tab      38.52\tab   37.45\tab    -2.78\par  Peso\tab      41.25\tab   40.20\tab    -2.55\par  Rupiah\tab  7970.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -12.48\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Desk 