\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Perky as dollar/yen retreats. \b0\par\par\uc2 852 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2000\par 04:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 5 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  perked up in early trade on Friday as the yen regained some \par \par \uc2  ground against the dollar. \par \par \uc2      Trade had not been affected by a computer virus dubbed the \par \par \uc2  "Love Bug" which wreaked havoc on computer systems around the \par \par \uc2  world on Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar retreated to the upper end of 107 yen\tab     due\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to a major offer from one U.S. bank overnight, which moved the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market in trade thinned by a long holiday in Japan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The (yen's) rebound was caused by a combination of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deal and thin trade. I don't think it signifies a reversal of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar's recent bullish trend," said a dealer at a European\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro\tab   managed to tick up slightly in early Asian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading after sagging to all-time lows against most major\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  overnight.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market is focused on U.S. non-farm payrolls data, due\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par later on Friday for clues on how aggressive the Federal Reserve\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are likely to be at their May 16 policy meeting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah remained steady on the stronger side of 8,000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar with dealers mostly sidelined amid continuing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par political uncertainty.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said better prospects for the IMF's delayed $400\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million loan were positive for the rupiah but the sacking of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par two ministers last week and the unrest in troubled Aceh\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par province cast doubt over its prospects.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "On the macro perspective, over the next six months or\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par towards the year-end, I'm looking for a weaker rupiah, probably\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 8,500 or 9,000," one dealer at a major bank said. Dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pinpointed its support at 8,035 and resistance at 7,900.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar edged higher in early Asian trading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but dealers expected it to trade in a range of 1.7150-1.7250\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the day as the market lacked strong incentives.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the Sing dollar was still hostage to major\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Given the beleaguered euro and the weakness in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/yen, the bias was likely to stay on its downside, they\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But continued caution over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would limit its losses.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is closed on Friday for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Children's Day holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won fell against the dollar on Thursday, weighed by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen's slide and dollar short-covering, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market will reopen on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso tracked the baht lower, with interbank and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate players bidding for dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market barely drew support from slightly lower than\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected April inflation data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Philippine annual inflation in April was 3.7 percent,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compared with 3.3 percent in March. The figure came in below\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 4.01 percent forecast in a Reuters poll of 10 economists.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht headed lower in sluggish offshore trade as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic markets were closed for the Coronation Day holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dipped through the key support of 38.50 before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bouncing back on dollar profit taking and offers left by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exporters before the holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht is expected to retain its weak tone in the near\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par term amid active dollar demand from offshore players and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par especially after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Thursday it had not\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to prop it up despite a recent sharp\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par drop.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It is like an invitation to sell. If the baht fails to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hold above the 38.50 level. The next target would be 38.65,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said a dealer at a U.S. bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar nudged up in sympathy with the yen as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan and Japan compete in similar export markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept investors cautious.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the government was unlikely to allow\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the unit to weaken beyond 30.70.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market was focused on local stocks after the Finance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Ministry announced measures to help cash-strapped firms.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers expected the moves to support the stock market,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attract inflows and subsequently boost the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0201 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     107.87\tab  108.62\tab    +0.70\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7197\tab  1.7225\tab    +0.16\par  Taiwan dlr    30.682\tab  30.689\tab    +0.02\par  Korean won   1111.00\tab 1111.00\tab    +0.00\par  Baht\tab      38.40\tab   38.51\tab    +0.29\par  Peso\tab      41.26\tab   41.09\tab    -0.41\par  Rupiah\tab  7