\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Dollar strength clouds regionals. \b0\par\par\uc2 784 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2000\par 11:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 3 (Reuters) - Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained \par \par \uc2  under pressure from broad-based dollar strength late on \par \par \uc2  Thursday in trade thinned by the absence of Tokyo players. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro\tab     hit new lows against the dollar and the\par \par sterling\tab      on capital outflows and persistent bearish\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment, before bouncing back slightly after dealers said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they saw European central banks buying euros for dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite the recent carnage, economists surveyed by Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par see the euro at 96.00 cents on average in one month, at 99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cents in three months and $1.03 in six months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar managed to hold above 109 yen\tab  , with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par chartists citing strong support at 108.20 where heavy bargain\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hunting was expected to emerge.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A drop below 107 would reverse the current bullish trend,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won retreated against the dollar but was still within\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its recent range, with the yen's easier tone and dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-covering keeping it on the defensive, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision to keep its target for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overnight call rate unchanged at 5.0 percent had little impact\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the market as the move had been widely anticipated.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht drifted near the intraday low of 38.47 as dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bids from offshore players outpaced exporter offers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said further losses should be limited due to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par technical factors as the unit was heavily oversold on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 14-day relative strength index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could rebound to 38.25 and then 38.15 in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par near-term while 38.50 remained a solid support, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah managed to keep its firm tone as the market grew\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more optimistic that the IMF would soon disburse a delayed $400\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million loan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah strengthened to 7,950 per dollar and managed to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hover around there for much of the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In the near-term, one analyst expected it to trade between\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par technical support at 8,050 and resistance at 7,943 but warned\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that the bias was more on the downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Despite the strength, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will still likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par follow the rest of the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eventually. And we\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par see that those \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are weaker," she said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar was mixed on Thursday but dealers said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the general mood was more bearish, though fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  put a floor on the downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The Sing dollar seems overly weak. There's a high chance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that the MAS (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) would\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," one analyst said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SEB Merchant Banking said in its daily report that it would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expect interbank selling to push the Singapore dollar back into\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the range of 1.7170-1.7220.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso's reprieve as a result of government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and rate hike talk proved short-lived.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The unit tracked the regionals lower, weighed by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar's strength and an absence of buying incentives, dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Market players expected the peso to trade between 41.20 and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 41.28 per dollar in the near-term with 41.40 in sight if it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par broke the bottom of that range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar regained some ground against the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar on the back of strong foreign direct investment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers see more room for a rise given that the U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was trading in overbought territory, with a reading of 72 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 14-day relative strength index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Moreover, a sharp decline in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unlikely as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was determined to defend it to eliminate any\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market expectations of a depreciation ahead of the official\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inauguration of the new government, dealers in Taipei said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0903 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     109.37\tab  108.85\tab    -0.48\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7232\tab  1.7187\tab    -0.26\par  Taiwan dlr    30.689\tab  30.693\tab    +0.01\par  Korean won   1111.20\tab 1109.80\tab    -0.13\par  Baht\tab      38.48\tab   38.29\tab    -0.49\par  Peso\tab      41.26\tab   41.27\tab    +0.02\par  Rupiah\tab  7970.00\tab 8015.00\tab    +0.56\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.37\tab  102.21\tab    -6.55\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7232\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.44\par  Taiwan dlr    30.689\tab  31.380\tab    +2.25\par  Korean won   1111.20\tab 1135.00\tab    +2.14\par  Baht\tab      38.48\tab   37.45\tab    -2.68\par  Peso\tab    