\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Easier, rates,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in focus. \b0\par\par\uc2 883 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2000\par 11:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , May 3 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  mostly easier in late trade on Wednesday as market participants \par \par \uc2  shifted focus to domestic factors in the absence of Tokyo \par \par \uc2  trade. \par \par \uc2      Activity in the Korean won and Philippine peso was \par \par \uc2  dominated by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and speculation about \par \par \uc2  potential rate hikes. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah\tab     pulled back and managed to stay above the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 8,000 level, buoyed by optimism that the IMF will soon release\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a delayed loan worth $400 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro\tab     sank to new lows below 90 cents against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar during European trade amid persistent pessimism about\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the European economy relative to the U.S. economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Prospects of an aggressive Federal Reserve tightening at its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par May 16 policy meeting supported the dollar against other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par majors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah was hovering just above the 8,000 per dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level as the market awaited the signing of Indonesia's latest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par letter of intent to the IMF, paving the way for the release of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a delayed $400 million loan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Earlier, chief economics minister Kwik Kian Gie said he was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par healthy and had no plans to quit the cabinet despite a health\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par scare and speculation he may be sacked.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Financial markets have been nervous about the stability of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par President Abdurrahman Wahid's ruling coalition after he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par abruptly dismissed two of his four economic ministers last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won ended flat after heavy dollar offers from exporters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were countered by bids from corporate players.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market was reluctant to push the won higher in the face\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of persistent state bank dollar bids and the Finance Ministry's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par repeated warnings against a rise in the won.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Bank of Korea holds its monthly monetary policy meeting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Thursday amid fading expectations of a rate hike following\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par benign April inflation data and worries Hyundai Investment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trust's woes might trigger instability in financial markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was propped up by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the face of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a worsening peace and order situation in the southern Mindanao\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par region.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said it was also lifted by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par comment that it might raise overnight rates again if the Fed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hikes rates by 50 basis points on May 16.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised overnight rates by 25 basis points\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on May 2 -- the first time in 10 months -- to make the peso\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more attractive.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The trend also reflected in the local bond market, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  two-year T-bond fetching a coupon of 11.75 percent at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday's auction, up from 11.5 percent at last month's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par auction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht slid against the dollar, under pressure from heavy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sales from investment houses and dollar short-covering demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some offers were believed to be linked to George Soros'\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Quantum Fund which is said to be unloading Asian assets as part\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the restructuring of its $8.5 billion fund.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Charts suggest the baht could head toward 38.65 if the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 38.50 level is broken.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar weakened but was off earlier lows,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressured by sliding stocks and political uncertainties.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said with less than three weeks away from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par official inauguration of the new government, China is unlikely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to reduce its pressure on Taiwan over the "one-China"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par principle.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The unit drew only limited support from comments from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Moody's Investors Service that its outlook for Taiwan Aa3\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign and local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ratings remains stable despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent political uncertainties.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Moody's said the ratings outlook for Taiwan will be most\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par immediately determined by economic, rather than by political\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par developments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar edged lower, slipping towards the 1.72\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level though the market was wary of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after coming up against persistent dollar bids from local banks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par above that level in mid-April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Standard Chartered said in a daily report that Singapore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities were likely to remain on guard against signs of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par imported inflation given rising business costs and oil prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chartists said dollar/Sing was looking a bit overbought on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 14-day relative strength index after breaking above an upward\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trend channel that's been in place since April 20.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The next key resistance for the dollar will be its March\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high of 1.7275.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0939 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     108.72\tab  108.54\tab    -0.17\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7185\tab  1.7162\tab    -0.13\par  Taiwan dlr    30.693\tab  30.669\tab    -0.08\par  Korean won   1109.80\tab 1109.90\tab    +0.01\par  Baht\tab      38.38\tab   38.29\tab    -0.23\par  Peso\tab      41.09\tab   41.27\tab    +0.44\par  Rupiah\tab  7940.00\tab 8015.00\tab    +0.94\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     108.72\tab  102.21\tab    -5.99\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7185\tab  1.6640\tab    -3.17\par  Taiwan dlr    30.693\tab  31.380\tab    +2.24\par  Korean won   1109.80\tab 1135.00\tab    +2.27\par  Baht\tab      38.38\tab   37.45\tab    -2.42\par  Peso\tab      41.09\tab   40.20\tab    -2.17\par  Rupiah\tab  7940.00\tab 6975.00\tab   -12.15\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Desk (65) 870-3087\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par email:asia.\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 @reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5301t1d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
