\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Slightly Down Late On US Dlr Strength \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2000\par 11:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar drifted lower in sluggish dealing late Wednesday in reaction to U.S. dollar strength against world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar approached the key level of S$1.7200 to the U.S. dollar, but dealers said it wasn't likely to break through it. \par \par \uc2  In recent weeks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to keep the U.S. dollar from rising above S$1.7200. \par \par \uc2  Philip Wee, treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank, said the MAS is concerned that sustained Singapore dollar weakness could raise the cost of imported components for local industries. \par \par \uc2  Around 0855 GMT (4:55 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7184, up from S$1.7165 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is gaining against the euro, yen and other world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on expectations the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee will raise rates aggressively when it meets May 16. \par \par \uc2  Higher U.S. interest rates make U.S. dollar-denominated securities more attractive and lure foreign investment from countries where interest rates are lower. \par \par \uc2  On the Singapore dollar money market, longer-term rates also moved higher on expectations that U.S. rates would be raised, while the overnight rate fell slightly. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate was offered at 2.2500%, down from 2.3750% late Tuesday, while the three-month rate was offered at 2.5625%, up from 2.5000%. \par \par 