\par\par \b \uc2  Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Up Late; S&P Downgrade Hurts Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2  By Benjamin Pedley \par \uc2 664 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2000\par 10:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly higher late Tuesday, buoyed by a rebound in most regional bourses after a hammering a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  A recovery on Wall Street Monday after record points losses in major indexes Friday helped lift regional stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the exception of Jakarta equities and the rupiah, which both sank after Standard & Poor's Corp. downgraded Indonesia's credit rating. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average Monday rose 276.7 points to end at 10,582.5, while the technology-laden Nasdaq jumped 217.9 points to 3539.2. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta stocks and the rupiah fell after S&P cut its long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issuer credit rating on Indonesia to SD, or selective default, from CCC+, and lowered its short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issuer rating to SD from C. \par \par \uc2  While the downgrade was expected after the government last week rescheduled $5.8 billion worth of sovereign debt with the Paris Club of creditors, there was a "knee-jerk" response in financial markets, says a rupiah trader in Singapore, who declined to be named. \par \par \uc2  Syetarn Hansakul, East Asia analyst at WestLB, said the downgrade doesn't reflect sudden negative risks emerging. \par \par \uc2  "The original (Paris Club) loans are technically in default until banks are officially notified of the rescheduling, which will be done soon, therefore we expect rupiah weakness to be temporary," she said. \par \par \uc2  "Once the facts are clarified, the rupiah should head toward 7,600." \par \par \uc2  The dollar late in the day was quoted at 7,725 rupiah, up from IDR7,670 a day earlier. The JSX Composite Index fell 0.5% to 526.7 from 529.3. \par \par \uc2  Among the other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Singapore dollar was the standout performer as it surged to a two-month high late in the day against its U.S. counterpart at S$1.6970, up from S$1.7055 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said heavy buying of the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by European banks pushed it through the psychological level of S$1.7000 against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which market participants say \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week around S$1.7200 to support the local dollar, may be promoting a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bid to control inflation in the wake of much stronger than expected consumer price index data from the U.S. Friday. \par \par \uc2  It may also be providing liquidity to offset a spate of recent foreign acquisitions by companies including Singapore Airlines and Singapore Telecommunications, know as SingTel, traders say. \par \par \uc2  A 0.6% rise in the benchmark Straits Times Index of share prices to 2,010.7 after an 8.7% slump Monday also aided the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in the region, a 5.6% jump in the Korea Composite Stock Price Index, or Kospi, to 747.3 after an 11.6% fall a day earlier lifted the won. \par \par \uc2  Buying of South Korean bonds after a statement Monday by the Bank of Korea - the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - that it wouldn't tighten monetary policy also aided the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to market participants. \par \par \uc2  "Some institutional investors expanded their bond buying," said Kim Il-soo, a broker at Hyundai Securities Co. \par \par \uc2  The yield on three-year corporate bonds ended down seven basis points to 9.97% while the yield on three-year government bonds ended 11 basis points lower at 8.93%. \par \par \uc2  At the close of trade in Seoul, the dollar was quoted at 1,110.4 won, down from KRW1,113.8 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ended at NT$30.517 against the New Taiwan dollar from NT$30.555 previously. Against the Philippine peso, it closed at 41.175 pesos from PHP41.190 and against the Thai baht, it ended at 37.870 baht, down from THB37.885 previously, on solid stock market gains in each country. \par \par \uc2  -By Benjamin Pedley; 65-421-4485; ben.pedley@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4i01xx8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
