\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Higher On Reports Of MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 2000\par 11:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar jumped to its highest level against the U.S. dollar in nearly two weeks Friday following reports of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by local monetary authorities. \par \par \uc2  The rally began Thursday and a number of dealers said they believed it was the result of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The MAS, as a matter of policy doesn't comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the MAS began selling dollars at about the S$1.7195 level, which was near the top of the recent trading range for the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The alleged MAS action in turn put pressure on market players who had taken long U.S. dollar positions, dealers said. The ensuing dollar selling pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an intraday low of S$1.7108 Friday, the lowest level since S$1.7103 on April 3. \par \par \uc2  "I doubt anyone will go long with the U.S. dollar now," a dealer at a foreign bank said. "The MAS is sending a message." \par \par \uc2  By the close, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered slightly to S$1.7115, down from $1.7152 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said the timing of the supposed MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was puzzling, since the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar didn't appear to be unusually soft. \par \par \uc2  But there was also speculation that the MAS did it as a preemptive move to head off what it may have perceived as a trend toward a weaker Singapore dollar. The timing was calculated, the theory goes, to take advantage of the long U.S. dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 3.2500%, up from 1.8750% late Thursday. The three-month rate was offered at 2.4375%, up from 2.3750%. \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Yonan Jr. 65-421-4859; alan.yonan@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4e01x1y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
