\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Late; Paris Club Hopes Buoy Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2  By Benjamin Pedley \par \uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 2000\par 11:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed late Thursday in lackluster trade as many financial market participants hugged the sidelines ahead of key U.S. inflation data. \par \par \uc2  Activity was also restricted by a holiday in Thailand and a parliamentary election in South Korea, where financial markets were shut for the day. \par \par \uc2  U.S. producer price index and consumer price index data - slated for release Thursday and Friday - will be watched closely for clues as to how much further the Federal Reserve needs to up interest rates to keep inflation in check. \par \par \uc2  Higher U.S. rates may place downward pressure on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly those - such as the Singapore dollar - which have yields below the Fed funds rate, which now stands at 6%. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah ended firmer on expectations the Paris Club of creditors will later Thursday agree to restructure $2.1 billion of Indonesian sovereign debt maturing this year. \par \par \uc2  "There is a high hope that Indonesia will get much of the debts rescheduled on favorable terms," said Syetarn Hansakul, an analyst at WestLB. "Positive news on this front could push the rupiah toward IDR7,500 (against the dollar)," she added. \par \par \uc2  Around 0920 GMT (5:20 a.m. EST), the dollar was at IDR7,600, down from IDR7,620 a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment remains bullish toward the won on expectations incumbent President Kim Dae-jung will retain enough parliamentary support to push through further economic reforms. Voting has ended and exit polls show Kim's Millennium Democratic Party holding a slight lead. \par \par \uc2  Kim's party faces the challenge of maintaining control of the 273-seat assembly as recent opinion polls had it trailing by about 10 seats. But many analysts believe the first-ever summit between the two Koreas, announced Monday, has tipped the scale toward the ruling party. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended Wednesday at 1,108.0 won, down from KRW1,109.4. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in North Asia, the New Taiwan dollar fell sharply as foreigners dumped local stocks after another sharp selloff in the Nasdaq Composite Index, and a fall in the Dow Jones Industrial Average. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan stock index ended down 2.5% at 9662.60, while the New Taiwan dollar finished the session at NT$30.380 to the U.S. dollar from NT$30.303 a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar rose slightly, helped by rumors the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in the day to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around S$1.7200 against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at S$1.7145 late, down from S$1.7180 previously. \par \par \uc2  With Thai markets closed, the baht rose in thin offshore trade. The dollar ended at 37.900 baht, down from THB38.020 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the dollar fell to 41.155 pesos from PHP41.175 with traders citing a fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peso around PHP41.200 and strength in the baht for the rise. \par \par \uc2  -By Benjamin Pedley; 65 421 4485; ben.pedley@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4d01vo7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
