\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Closes Up After Tracking Yen Vs US Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2000\par 11:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was stronger late Wednesday after a day of tracking movements in the U.S. dollar against the yen. \par \par \uc2  At about 0855 GMT (4:55 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7188, down from S$1.7197 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was at Y105.49, down sharply from Y106.45 late Tuesday in Asia and from Y106.99 in New York. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said there was little in the way of domestic news to move the Singapore dollar, which was left to track the dollar-yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen rose following remarks by Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami, which appeared to suggest that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is considering ending its zero-interest rate policy. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar briefly rose to an intraday high of S$1.7210, the area where the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is considered likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , before falling back. Its decline from that peak coincided with its slide against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Singapore dollar is likely to continue tracking the dollar-yen. If the U.S. dollar moves below Y105, they said, it could also fall to the level of S$1.7155. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 1.6250%, down from 1.750% late Tuesday. The three-month rate was offered at 2.3750%, up from 2.3125%. \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4c01w2e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\pi