\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Little Changed Early Ahead Of G7 Meeting \b0\par\par\uc2 678 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2000\par 03:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are little changed against the U.S. dollar in early regional trading Wednesday, as market participants remain cautious ahead of this weekend's meeting of the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations. \par \par \uc2  Trading is relatively light with market participants apparently reluctant to go too far out on a limb given the uncertainty over what G7 leaders may say about exchange rates, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  There is speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets that the G7 countries could offer a statement expressing their concern over the strength of the yen. That talk already has translated into support for the dollar, with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rising above 107 yen in overnight trading for the first time in more than two weeks. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah edged downward, but remains well above the six-month low hit last week. The rupiah has been boosted by optimism that the Paris Club donor nations may reschedule $2.1 billion in foreign debt when the group meets beginning Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The possibility that Indonesia will get favorable terms from the Paris Club was increased after it met nine out of 14 reform targets sought by the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  A positive scenario could push the U.S. dollar below the IDR7,500 level in the near term, WestLB Bank said in its daily commentary. \par \par \uc2  At 0120 GMT (9 p.m. EDT Tuesday) the dollar was quoted at 7,623 rupiah, up slightly from IDR7,615 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar fell slightly against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but remained at the higher end of the recent trading range. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts say recent pressure on the Singapore dollar was triggered by a slew of foreign acquisitions by local companies that need to buy U.S. dollars to finance the deals. Others, however, say \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  commitments for such acquisitions are probably worked through the market in advance, and therefore have minimal impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  Nonetheless, many analysts remain bearish on the Singapore dollar in the near term. Concerns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent excessive depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped stabilize the unit. However, DBS Bank said a testing of the S$1.7250 resistance level couldn't be ruled out. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7187, down from $1.7197 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the Thai baht was exceptionally thin, dealers said, as markets prepared to close Thursday and Friday for the annual Songkran water festival. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar was quoted at 30.040 baht, unchanged from Tuesday's\par close.\par - - 12/04/00 01-40G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In North Asia, the South Korean won remained in a tight range ahead of\par Thursday's general election.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market could get a short-term boost if the ruling Millennium\par Democratic Party is able to garner more votes than expected, DBS bank\par said. But the sentiment may not be as buoyant heading into the medium\par term due to the slow pace of reforms, DBS added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Whatever the outcome, continuing inflows of foreign direct investment\par are expected to continue to support the won, despite a narrowing trade\par surplus, DBS said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was quoted at 1,109.5 won, little changed from KRW1,109.4\par late Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The New Taiwan dollar slipped after Tuesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ended a three-day rally for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par of China sold the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively in a move to clamp down on\par speculators.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was quoted at NT$30.325, up from NT$30.307 the\par previous session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A dealer said the pair are expected to trade in a range of NT$30.280\par to NT$30.350.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso is likely to remain range-bound as banks replenish\par their dollar supplies after experiencing ample corporate demand, traders\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was quoted at 41.132 pesos, up from PHP41.120 late Tuesday.\par     -By Alan Yonan Jr. 65-421-4859; alan.yonan@dowjones.com\par -0- 12/04/00 02-03G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4c01vi5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
