\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Late Morning On Overseas Acquisitions \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2000\par 05:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar is lower late morning Tuesday on the heels of a weaker yen and continuing reports of overseas acquisitions by local firms. \par \par \uc2  At 0305 GMT (11:05 p.m. EDT Monday) the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7192, up from S$1.7165 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The latest deal would have the Government of Singapore Investment Corp. acquire a stake in Indonesia's Bank Central Asia, according to a report in the Singapore's Business Times. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesia Bank Restructuring Agency, which owns 92.8% of BCA, hopes to raise US$200 million through an initial public offering. IBRA reportedly approached the GIC about buying a "significant stake" in BCA. \par \par \uc2  Also Tuesday, Singapore Airlines Ltd. confirmed that it has bought an 8.3% stake in Air New Zealand. In another recently announced deal, Singapore Telecommunications Ltd. said it would move ahead with its purchase of a stake in Time Engineering Bhd. of Malaysia for more than S$1 billion. \par \par \uc2  Such acquisitions by Singapore private and government-linked companies often put pressure on the Singapore dollar because the require local companies to sell the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market to finance the deals. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the U.S. dollar to trade between S$1.7130 and S$1.7190 Tuesday. The pair are unlikely to go above S$1.7200, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shown an apparent willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Alan Yonan Jr. 65-421-4859; alan.yonan@dowjones.com\par -0- 11/04/00 03-10G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4b01txn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
