\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Ends Down, In Line With Yen; Range Trade Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2000\par 11:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar ended lower in sluggish trading Monday in line with the yen's decline against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At about 0915 GMT (5:15 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7188, up from S$1.7125 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the U.S. dollar to continue trading in a range of between S$1.7100 and S$1.7200 in coming days. "It's not really going anywhere," one dealer said of the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's gains are likely to be capped at the top end of the range by the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was said to have sold U.S. dollars last week in a bid to limit the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's losses, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar could break out its range if the U.S. dollar breaks through the resistance level of Y108 against the yen, dealers said. If that happens, the U.S. dollar could trade above S$1.7200, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Flows of funds out of the country by Singapore companies buying foreign assets have depressed the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But a preliminary pact to buy 14.5% of Malaysia's Time Engineering by Singapore Telecommunications, announced Friday, has already been discounted by the market, said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  SingTel is expected to pay about US$580 million for the Time Engineering stake as well as stakes of 20% in each of the latter's Internet and telecommunications subsidiaries. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 1.6250%, down from 2.5000% late Friday. The three-month rate was offered at 2.3125%, up from 2.2500%. \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4a01toa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
