\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Higher Amid Rally In Regional  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2000\par 05:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar is higher midmorning Friday in line with a firmer tone in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets across the region. \par \par \uc2  Market participants were reluctant to have excessive exposure to long U.S. dollar positions, with the yen continuing to strengthen, a dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is below Y105 and it's looking to test the downside," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also enjoyed support from a stronger stock market. The Straits Times Index is up 1.5% at midmorning. \par \par \uc2  At 0315 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at S$1.7124, down from S$1.7156 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Market participants are keeping an eye on developments in Singapore Telecommunications Ltd's bid to buy a stake in Malaysia's Time Engineering Bhd, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  If Singtel has to sell local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to complete the transaction, it could weigh on the Singapore dollar, a dealer at a foreign bank said. However, if Singtel pays in ringgit that it may already hold, the deal would have little impact on the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said he expected the U.S. dollar to trade against the Singapore unit in a range of S$1.7120 to S$1.7180, with the upper limit being capped by concerns of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The MAS entered the market on Wednesday to stem a decline in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Yonan Jr. 65-421-4859; alan.yonan@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4701tan\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
