\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Stronger On Array Of Local Factors \b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2000\par 03:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are stronger against the U.S. dollar early Friday, dictated mostly by local factors, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah, which has been under selling pressure in recent sessions, regained some ground as the government made preparations to sell the assets of what was once the country's largest private bank. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency will launch an international roadshow next week in Singapore to find buyers for the assets of Bank Central Asia. \par \par \uc2  Prospects for a successful sale buoyed investor sentiment in the rupiah, a dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  At 0130 GMT (9:30 p.m. EDT Thursday) the dollar was quoted at 7,720 rupiah, down from IDR7,785 late Thursday in thin offshore trading. Indonesian markets were closed Thursday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had been bid up as high as IDR7,800 earlier in the week on concerns that Indonesia may fail to meet International Monetary Fund reform deadline this Saturday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar continued to strengthen following alleged government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets Wednesday to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7132, down from S$1.7156 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Market participants are keeping an eye on developments in Singapore Telecommunications Ltd.'s bid to buy a stake in Malaysia's Time Engineering Bhd., dealers said. \par \par \uc2  If SingTel has to sell local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to complete the transaction, it could weigh on the Singapore dollar, a dealer at a foreign bank said. However, if SingTel pays in ringgit that it may already hold, the deal would have little impact on the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said he expected the U.S. dollar to trade against the Singapore unit in a range of S$1.7120 to S$1.7180, with the upper limit being capped by concerns of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht moved higher as exporters entered the market to sell dollars, a dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was quoted at 38.000 baht, down from THB38.135 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The baht could come under some selling pressure later in the day if market participants and corporations buy the U.S. dollar for position squaring and to cover their liquidity needs in advance of next week's market closing for the Thai new year, analysts at WestLB Research said. \par \par \uc2  In North Asia, the South Korean won moved higher as investors poured money into local stocks. The market's benchmark Korea Composite Stock Price Index was up 2.5% at midmorning. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 1,110.90 won, down from KRW1,112.0 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar was slightly higher, although continued outflows of foreign equity funds were expected to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under pressure, a dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was quoted at NT$30.451, down from NT$30.469 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Against the Philippine peso, the dollar was quoted at PHP41.090, down from PHP41.120 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Yonan Jr. 65-421-4859; alan.yonan@dowjones.com 07/04/00 02-35G \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4701t8e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
