\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Directionless, U.S. stocks eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,005 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2000\par 11:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, April 6 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  were directionless in late trade on Thursday as a few markets \par \par \uc2  were closed and investors awaited direction from Wall Street. \par \par \uc2      Onshore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in Thailand and Indonesia were \par \par \uc2  closed for public holidays and trade was done from offshore \par \par \uc2  centers. \par \par \uc2      Malaysia was also closed. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar drifted in a tight range against the yen\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as the prospects of further wild gyrations in U.S. stocks kept\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors sidelined.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro\tab     managed to hold within a quarter-point\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range above the key psychological level of $0.96, supported by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculation the Group of Seven nations may take a tougher\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stance in aid of the weak euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Merrill Lynch expected some broad-based US dollar weakness\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to develop during the second quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     This reflected growing current account financing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par difficulties and relative underperformance of U.S. financial\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par assets as the Federal Reserve further tightened monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par policy, it said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We continue to look for a three percent depreciation in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the trade-weighted dollar over the next 12 months," Merrill\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said in its report.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON\tab     -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won rebounded from early losses on dollar offers from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate players and foreign stocks funds despite sharp falls\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in local stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of Korea Governor Chon Chol-hwan said on Thursday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflationary pressure has yet to emerge and an inflation target\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 3.1 percent for this year would not be difficult to meet.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But he added that rising prices could threaten inflation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par targets beginning next year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some analysts expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to tighten monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par policy in the second quarter of this year either by raising\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rates or allowing the won to appreciate due to rising\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflationary pressure.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah clung to its lowest levels in around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par five-and-a-half months in paper-thin offshore trade. Domestic\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and stock markets were closed for the Moslem New Year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the dollar was likely to remain well-bid when\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the domestic market re-opens on Friday amid fears the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government may fail to meet International Monetary Fund (IMF)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reform deadlines this Saturday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Top economics minister Kwik Kian Gie has said some of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reforms linked to the recapitalisation of state banks and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par private-sector debt restructuring would be completed on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Saturday and others by the following Saturday - April 15.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia's official Antara news agency reported on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday that the IMF had expressed confidence the country\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would meet its deadlines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore kept to a relatively narrow 1.7120 to 1.7161\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par band, with dealers wary of chasing dollar/Sing above 1.7200\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par levels in case local banks \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been defending the Sing dollar at around 1.72/1.73 levels in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent weeks though no confirmation was available.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One dealer from a European bank said dollars were likely to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remain well bid in the near-to-medium term due to talk of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possible foreign acquisitions by local companies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Even if such moves could be funded by share swap options\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rather than cash, it does effect sentiment," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Business Times newspaper said Singapore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Telecommunications Ltd  had agreed to buy 14.5 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Malaysian telecommunications company Time Engineering Bhd\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SingTel shares were down one cent at S$2.34 while Time\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Engineering shares were down 10 cents at 5.85 ringgit at 0812\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar ended easier, but off intraday lows, amid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outflows by foreign equity funds and commercial dollar demand\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from state-run enterprises.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taipei dealers said some foreign equity funds had taken\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par profit in better performers like Taiwan in the wake of stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corrections elsewhere.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign funds sold a net T$1.126 billion in Taiwan equities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Thursday after selling T$3.257 worth the previous day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The TAIEX\tab      ended 2.13 percent lower, under the key\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10,000 point mark.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht trade was active in the morning although the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par onshore market was closed for Chakri Memorial holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The unit slipped through the strong support of 38.00 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar demand from foreign names.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the market was caught short of dollars as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offers made earlier this week was overdone.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Players are covering their short dollar positions ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the long Songkran festival -- the Thai traditional New Year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par holiday -- starting April 13.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers see 38.20 as a good support for now. Investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were expected to sell dollars on a rally to that level, but a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par break above it could lead the baht to fall to 38.40.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso retained its soft tone but with the downside\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supported by fears of potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar-buying\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Even though the peso is one of a few high yielding\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region, investors were reluctant to invest in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the unit in a significant way due to the country's shaky\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic and political outlook, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The near-term support is seen at 41.20 for now.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0854 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     104.67\tab  105.30\tab    +0.60\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7133\tab  1.7175\tab    +0.25\par  Taiwan dlr    30.469\tab  30.465\tab    -0.01\par  Korean won   1111.70\tab 1114.50\tab    +0.25\par  Baht\tab      38.08\tab   37.99\tab    -0.24\par  Peso\tab      41.11\tab   41.10\tab    -0.02\par  Rupiah\tab  7770.00\tab 7760.00\tab    -0.13\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7999\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     104.67\