\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Higher Late After Reported MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2000\par 11:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar moved higher late Thursday, a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reportedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A local bank was seen selling U.S. dollars against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in late Asian trading Wednesday in a move that had all the markings of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The action triggered dollar selling in the London market, pushing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down from a one-month high of S$1.7240 to levels around S$1.7120. \par \par \uc2  Dollar demand pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back up to S$1.7140 near the end of the trading day, but it was still down from S$1.7185 the late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The MAS apparently was uncomfortable about the decline in the Singapore dollar against the trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  it uses as a benchmark, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "If you use that calculation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket was slightly overshooting their usual tolerance," said Alison Seng, an analyst at Standard & Poor's MMS. \par \par \uc2  The market will retain a bias for U.S. dollar demand in the near-term, she said, based on expectations that Singapore companies will continue selling the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to acquire foreign companies. \par \par \uc2  Furthermore, concerns over the political and economic situations in Indonesia and Thailand will weigh on the Singapore dollar, she said. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 1.5000%, up from 1.2500% late Wednesday. The three-month rate was offered at 2.3125%, up from 2.2500%. \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Yonan Jr. 65-421-4850; alan.yonan@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4601ryt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
