\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Higher After Monetary Authorities  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2000\par 04:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is higher midmorning Thursday following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by local monetary authorities overnight to halt a decline in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar, dealers and analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Economic fundamentals remain positive for the Singapore dollar, analysts said, noting Wednesday's selling of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was more technical in nature. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore spokesman said it is the agency's policy not to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Dealers, however, said the MAS entered the market Wednesday in London and New York after a drop in the Singapore dollar triggered stop loss orders that threatened to push the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its lowest level for the year. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had fallen during Asian trading hours, continued its decline in London as market participants looked to cover their short positions in U.S. dollars. Once the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to S$1.7189 the stop loss orders were triggered and the unit quickly jumped to S$1.7225, prompting the MAS to step in, a dealer at a U.S. brokerage said. \par \par \uc2  "They didn't want the Singapore dollar to hit a new low for the year based on technical selling," he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0230 GMT (10:30 p.m. EDT Wednesday) the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7148, down from S$1.7185 late Wednesday in Asian trading. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a foreign bank said he expected the pair to trade in a range of S$1.7135 to S$1.7180, with concerns over further MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limiting the topside. \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Yonan Jr. 65-421-4859; alan.yonan@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw4601r8a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
