\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Late;Follows Rupiah Lower In Quiet Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 11:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar, searching for direction in listless trading, was lower late Wednesday, following the Indonesian rupiah lower. \par \par \uc2  However, declines in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar were limited as investors remain generally bullish on the Singapore economy and the prospects for continued growth. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7158 late Wednesday, up from S$1.7145 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar opened the day on the defensive against the U.S. dollar, but recovered somewhat after its initial decline. The pair traded in a fairly narrow range for he balance of the day. \par \par \uc2  The main culprit in the drop in the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the faltering rupiah in neighboring Indonesia. The rupiah came under pressure when the release of its next loan installment from the International Monetary Fund was delayed. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar touched an intraday high of S$1.7172 but market participants were reluctant to bid it up higher on fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a trader at a Japanese Bank said. \par \par \uc2  The pair are expected to trade in a range of S$1.7130 to S$1.7190 in the near term with the latter representing the likely trigger point for MAS action, he said. \par \par \uc2  The longer-term outlook for the Singapore dollar remains bullish, traders said, with expectations the government will take in several billion dollars from the sale of telecommunications licenses beginning April 1. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 1.8750%, up from 1.6259% late Tuesday. The three-month rate was offered at 2.5333%, up from 2.3125%. \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Yonan Jr. 65-421-4859; alan.yonan@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3t01lhw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
