\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Of America Lowers S$ Forecast To S$1.60/USD By Yr-End \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 13:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Bank of America on Tuesday revised its forecast for the Singapore dollar exchange rate downward to S$1.60 to the U.S. dollar by year-end from S$1.51 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The recent weakness of the Singapore dollar has confounded a number of forecasts, including that of the Bank of America. The U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7168 late Thursday, up from S$1.6655 at the end of last year. \par \par \uc2  Bank of America had argued that incipient inflation, along with sustained economic recovery, would prompt Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tighten monetary policy by allowing the Singapore dollar to appreciate. \par \par \uc2  The exchange rate is the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's sole monetary policy tool. A stronger Singapore dollar stifles inflation by reducing prices of imported goods. \par \par \uc2  The MAS recently revised the January annual inflation figure downward to 0.9% from 1.5%, based on a reweighted basket of consumer goods and services. In February, the inflation rate, based on the new basket, rose to an annual 1.3%. \par \par \uc2  With inflation on a lower path than previously expected, the pressure to tighten monetary policy has eased, Bank of America said in a report. \par \par \uc2  "The latest CPI number suggests there is little pressure for monetary tightening at present," the report says. \par \par \uc2  But the report also cites recent rumors that the MAS has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. "This suggests that the present period of looseness may have run its course," the report says. \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3s01m97\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
