\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Gives Up Gains To End Little Changed \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 10:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar ended little changed in calm dealing Tuesday after giving up intraday gains, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At about 0835 GMT (3:35 am EST), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7156, up marginally from S$1.7152 late Monday and higher than an intraday low of S$1.7121. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  started out strong, maintaining its momentum from Monday, when rumors of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  propelled it upward against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also reported a smattering of Singapore-dollar purchases by investors putting money into the local equities market. \par \par \uc2  Seeking to take advantage of its gains, some participants sold the U.S. dollar short early in the day, only to be caught flat-footed by a larger order to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One dealer identified Citibank as the buyer, but a dealer there declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  Later in the day, the Singapore dollar continued to inch downward, following the path set by the Indonesian rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is likely to stay within its recent range of between S$1.7100 and S$1.7200, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, one dealer said that the U.S. dollar could test S$1.7200, the recent ceiling, if the euro weakens to US$0.95 in European trading later Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 1.625%, unchanged from late Monday. The three-month rate was offered at 2.3125% down from 2.375%. \par \par \uc2  -By Christopher Wellisz; 65/ 421-4802; christopher.wellisz@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3s01lxi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
