\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Ends Higher On Buying By Large Fund \b0\par\par\uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 11:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar ended stronger Monday after a large offshore fund sold U.S. dollars for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At about 0940 GMT (4:40 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7135, down from S$1.7149 late Friday and from a peak Monday of S$1.7191. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar weakened early Monday following Friday's announcement that a Singapore-led consortium had won a bid to buy a US$506 million stake in Indonesian auto-maker PT Astra International. \par \par \uc2  But during the lunchtime break, the U.S. dollar suddenly dropped nearly half a Singapore cent in thin dealing. Some dealers said they suspected that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from depreciating too quickly. \par \par \uc2  However, other dealers said that a major offshore fund had sold U.S. dollars for Singapore dollars in several transactions parceled out among local banks, possibly to buy equities on the Singapore Exchange. \par \par \uc2  "A large fund let go of some (U.S.) dollars," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, share prices on the stock market ended up 3.3% on Monday, boosted by program buying of blue-chip shares by foreign funds. Stock market dealers said bank and property shares had been oversold and were viewed as bargains. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were surprised by the timing of the lunch-time \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transaction, since thin liquidity exaggerated the speed of the Singapore dollar's gains. One dealer estimated the size of the transaction at US$200 million. \par \par \uc2  In addition, dealers said, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions associated with the Astra deal had already been completed, releiving the selling pressure on the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is likely to trade in a range S$1.7050 and S$1.7150 Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 1.6250%, down from 1.875% late Friday. The three-month rate was offered at 2.375%, down from 2.4375%. \par \par \uc2  -By Christopher Wellisz; 65/ 421-4802; christopher.wellisz@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3r01kui\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
