\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 :  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Saps Won;  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr  Down \b0\par\par\uc2 733 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 03:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The South Korean won has been pushed down on dollar-buying by a state-run bank in early trading Monday, but observers say the authorities have resigned themselves to a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the back of a resurgent economy. \par \par \uc2  The new Taiwan dollar is also gaining in early dealing Monday, propelled by continuing flows of foreign capital into the equity market. \par \par \uc2  In Southeast Asia, the Singapore dollar has been weakened by disappointing industrial production figures and by news that a Singapore-led consortium has taken a controlling stake in Indonesian carmaker PT Astra International. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah, meanwhile, is little changed, although some analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to gain as a result of the Astra sale, which will pump US$506 million into the state's coffers. \par \par \uc2  In Korea, U.S.-dollar buying by the state-run Korean Development Bank has pushed the won lower. In addition, reports that Korea Asset Management Corp. will buy US$1.95 billion of Daewoo Group foreign debt have also weakened the won. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts say that the Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's climb is inevitable as economic growth continues to pick up speed. \par \par \uc2  "The appreciation pressure on the won has been intensifying over the past few trading days," said David Simmonds, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank in Singapore. "There is little doubt in my mind that that pressure will prevail." \par \par \uc2  Simmonds said the Korean authorities have resigned themselves to a stronger won and will seek to maintain an orderly appreciation. \par \par \uc2  "There is an acceptance that the fundamentals justify - indeed, probably demand - a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a short period of time," he said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0150 GMT (8:50 p.m. EST Sunday), the U.S. dollar was trading at 1,109.80 won, up from KRW1,108.70 late Friday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar is also expected to continue climbing as more money flows into the stock market and concerns ease about the March 18 presidential election, which saw the victory of an opposition party that has espoused formal independence from China. \par \par \uc2  With the victorious Democratic Progressive Party moving toward abandoning its pro-independence stance, worries about strained relations with China have eased and investors have focused again on Taiwan's fast-growing economy. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has maintained a strong grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though, and will likely slow the rate of its appreciation and keep it within a tight trading range, observers say. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar was trading at NT$30.640, down from NT$30.664 late\par Friday.\par - - 27/03/00 01-56G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Southeast Asia, the Singapore dollar is weaker as a result of\par capital outflows associated with the purchase of a 40% stake in\par Indonesian carmaker PT Astra International by a Singapore-led\par consortium.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has also been weakened by disappointing industrial\par production data released Sunday. Manufacturing output rose 9.4% in\par February over the same month last year, down from January's year-on-year\par growth of 28.2%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, Simon Flint, an economist at Bank of America, said the\par weakness of the Singapore dollar is likely to be limited by the prospect\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . He said the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is approaching levels where the MAS has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the past.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah, meanwhile, is slightly weaker against the\par dollar, despite the Astra sale, which was seen as a boost for the\par cash-strapped government's asset-sale program.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's positive that they've managed to sell of these assets," Flint\par said. "They have received US$500 million. That's good for the economy\par and that's good for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Observers expect the rupiah to strengthen as the International\par Monetary Fund decides this week whether to dole out a further US$400\par million in aid.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Around 0215 GMT, the U.S. dollar is at S$1.7181, up from S$1.7149 late\par Friday. The U.S. dollar is at 7,485 rupiah, up from IDR7,451 late\par Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht and Philippine peso are slightly lower early Monday. The\par U.S. dollar is at 37.820 baht, up from THB37.760 late Friday. The U.S.\par dollar is at 40.950 pesos, up from PHP40.930 late Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Christopher Wellisz; 65/ 421-4802;\par christopher.wellisz@dowjones.com\par -0- 27/03/00 02-25G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3r01kht\par }\page {\par\