\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Stronger As Won Hits Post-Crisis High \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 635 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 09:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- Sustained foreign investor interest in South Korean assets coupled with inward trade flows Wednesday to drive the won to its highest level since November 1997. \par \par \uc2  Most other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also gained. Only the Thai baht slipped as traders unwound long positions established over the last week in anticipation of heavy foreign direct investment flows into Thailand. \par \par \uc2  The continued run-up in the won prompted repeated verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Korean finance officials, anxious that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rapid appreciation will dent the country's export sector. \par \par \uc2  Twice during the session the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy issued statements calling the won's rise "worrisome." The government is watching the market closely and is ready to take measures to slow the won's rise, the ministry warned. \par \par \uc2  Threats of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did little to damp the enthusiasm of won bulls, who noted comments from Finance Minister Lee Hun-jai stressing Korea's continued need for foreign investment. Further equity investment in Korean companies will help stabilize the country's highly leveraged corporate sector, Lee told reporters. \par \par \uc2  His remarks helped fuel heavy won purchases, which pushed the dollar down to KRW1,112.70 in intraday trading, the lowest the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has seen since November 27, 1997. \par \par \uc2  Although state-run banks were spotted buying dollars during the day, most market participants believe the government's intention is merely to slow, rather than to halt or reverse, the won's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  At the close the dollar was at KRW1,112.90, compared with KRW1,116.40 the previous session. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar also rose Wednesday, building on gains made the previous day, as investor sentiment continued to recover from the sell-off preceding and immediately following the weekend's presidential election. \par \par \uc2  At the close of trading in Taipei, the U.S. dollar was quoted at NT$30.711, down from NT$30.738 the day before. At $413 million, transaction volumes were less than one third the level seen during Monday's hectic session. \par \par \uc2  In Southeast Asia the Singapore dollar strengthened and the baht slipped back as dealers unwound long baht positions in the cross market. \par \par \uc2  "Over the last two days trading has been driven by a lot of talk about acquisitions, but most of it was on a preemptive, speculative basis," said a dealer at one U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Market players, who earlier in the week had bought baht for Singapore dollars on rumors that Singapore Airlines was in talks to buy a stake in Thai Airways and that HSBC was looking to acquire Bangkok Metropolitan Bank, moved to close out their positions Wednesday, pushing the Singapore dollar up and the baht down. \par \par \uc2  Talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was closely watching exchange rates also helped to boost the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as traders covered their short positions, afraid of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia the U.S. dollar was quoted against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at S$1.7138, down from S$1.7191 the previous day. Against the baht the dollar was at THB37.830, up from THB37.820. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah strengthened a touch, but traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still being capped by dollar demand from Indonesian corporations. Toward the end of Asian dealing the dollar was at IDR7,441, down from IDR7,461 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine Dealing System, the peso ended higher, with the dollar dropping to PHP40.895, from PHP40.963 the day before. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  SUBSCRIBERS CAN FIND ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  COMMENT ON: \par \par \uc2  TELERATE PAGES [1136] OR [4250] \par \par \uc2  DOW JONES NEWSWIRES BY SEARCHING THE CODE N/FXW \par \par \uc2  BLOOMBERG BY ENTERING NI FRX \par \par \uc2  REUTERS BY ENTERING CODE \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /DJ \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw3m01h86\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
