\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets - Regionals aloof to euro woes. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 1,117 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2000\par 10:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Feb 28 (Reuters) - The euro's breathless descent \par \par \uc2  to fresh life lows against the dollar had traders in Asia \par \par \uc2  transfixed on Monday, though most regional markets remained \par \par \uc2  impervious to the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plight. \par \par \uc2      Thin trading conditions and hedge selling of euro/yen by \par \par \uc2  Japanese institutional investors triggered stop-loss sales, \par \par \uc2  taking the euro to a record low of $0.9390, a 3.6 percent drop \par \par \uc2  on the day. \par \par \uc2      Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed it up to $0.9655 \par \par \uc2  by 0900 GMT while euro/yen was at 105.29 after falling as far \par \par \uc2  as 102.45, within a whisker of its life low of 102.05. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said there was little in the way of fresh factors \par \par \uc2  behind the move -- just a growing conviction the European \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't hike rates, coupled with Friday's \par \par \uc2  unexpectedly strong U.S. GDP numbers. \par \par \uc2      REGIONALS COOL TO EURO SHOCK \par \par \uc2      Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held their ground in the face of the \par \par \uc2  euro's drop, merely extending their early gains as the yen \par \par \uc2  headed higher against the dollar. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said this was hardly surprising, given that Japan \par \par \uc2  and the United States are Asia's main export markets. \par \par \uc2      They said the impact of the euro's moves was more likely to \par \par \uc2  be felt through the yen. \par \par \uc2      "The significant decline we've seen in euro/yen has brought \par \par \uc2  some incremental decline in dollar/yen and that can be manifest \par \par \uc2  in some renewed regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength against the dollar," \par \par \uc2  said David Simmonds, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  The yen's rise drove the Korean won through the 1,130 per \par \par \uc2  dollar barrier, but authorities were quick to express unease \par \par \uc2  with its strength and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly through state-run \par \par \uc2  banks. \par \par \uc2  Even the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, managed against a trade-weighted \par \par \uc2  basket believed to include the euro, took its cue from the \par \par \uc2  firmer yen and some robust economic data. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's industrial output rose 26.8 percent on the year \par \par \uc2  to January after December's 7.2 percent rise. It was up 17.3 \par \par \uc2  percent in January on a three-month moving average basis. \par \par \uc2  Evidence that Singapore's recovery was indeed on track \par \par \uc2  despite some poor export numbers last week, coupled with strong \par \par \uc2  chart support at 1.7120 would limit the Sing dollar's downside \par \par \uc2  in the near term, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  But some pointed out that its rise could also be capped \par \par \uc2  despite a pick-up in inflation and strong domestic \par \par \uc2  fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Barclays Capital said Singapore was unlikely to face a \par \par \uc2  monetary tightening until late in the second quarter, or \par \par \uc2  beyond. \par \par \uc2      "Despite the strength of recovery, the government remains \par \par \uc2  concerned that the base of recovery is narrow and relies on \par \par \uc2  strong export growth and a recovery in private consumption..., \par \par \uc2  which in turn was driven by a rally in the local stock market," \par \par \uc2  it said in a weekly report. \par \par \uc2      WALL STREET GNAWS AT ASIA STOCKS \par \par \uc2      Most Asian stock markets headed south in the wake of Wall \par \par \uc2  Street's losses on Friday, as investors worried that \par \par \uc2  unexpectedly strong U.S. growth would spur aggressive interest \par \par \uc2  rate hikes. \par \par \uc2      The Nikkei 225 lost nearly 0.5 percent due to the yen's \par \par \uc2  rise. \par \par \uc2      Korea's KOSPI closed at its lowest in four months, with key \par \par \uc2  telecom shares worst hit. \par \par \uc2      Manila shares were also down a hefty 4.13 percent as \par \par \uc2  worries about U.S. rate hikes were compounded by a perception \par \par \uc2  of growing cronyism in the administration of President Joseph \par \par \uc2  Estrada. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong shares lost out despite gains in China Telecom, \par \par \uc2  with investors still focused on merger talks between Pacific \par \par \uc2  Century CyberWorks (PCCW) and Cable & Wireless HKT Ltd. \par \par \uc2      C&W HKT said a deal between its parent, Britain's Cable & \par \par \uc2  Wireless Plc, and PCCW could be reached within 48 hours. \par \par \uc2      CHINA GROWTH ON TRACK \par \par \uc2      China affirmed its 1999 GDP growth forecast of 7.1 percent \par \par \uc2  and said it was looking for an even better performance this \par \par \uc2  year. \par \par \uc2      The State Statistical Bureau said the economy grew at a 6.8 \par \par \uc2  percent pace in the fourth quarter year-on-year to give a 7.1 \par \par \uc2  percent rate for the full year. \par \par \uc2      It said retail sales rose 6.8 percent year-on-year, while \par \par \uc2  industrial output steamed ahead by 8.5 percent. \par \par \uc2      Fixed asset investment was up 5.2 percent but foreign \par \par \uc2  direct investment dropped 11.4 percent. \par \par \uc2      Despite the strong growth, prices continued to drop. The \par \par \uc2  consumer price index fell 1.4 percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2      Growth this year was expected to at least match the 1999 \par \par \uc2  rate, and possibly surpass it, thanks to strong exports, the \par \par \uc2  government's commitment to active fiscal policy and its plan to \par \par \uc2  pour money into the poorer western hinterland. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0912 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     109.06\tab  110.89\tab    +1.68\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7093\tab  1.7085\tab    -0.05\par  Taiwan dlr    30.764\tab  30.785\tab    +0.07\par  Korean won   1134.00\tab 1136.00\tab    +0.18\par  Baht\tab      37.87\tab   37.95\tab    +0.21\par  Peso\tab      40.85\tab   40.80\tab    -0.12\par  Rupiah\tab  7440.00\tab 7425.00\tab    -0.20\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     109.06\tab  102.21\tab    -6.28\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7093\tab  1.6640\tab    -2.65\par  Taiwan dlr    30.764\tab  31.380\tab    +2.00\par  Korean won   1134.00\tab 1135.00\tab    +0.09\par  Baht\tab      37.87\tab   37.45\tab    -1.11\par  Peso\tab      40.85\tab   40.20\tab    -1.59\par  Rupiah\tab  7440.00\tab 6975.00\tab    -6.25\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7997\tab    -0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ASIAN STOCK MARKETS  0912 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Market\tab  Current\tab Prev Close     Pct Move\par  Tokyo\tab  19720.10     19817.88\tab    -0.49\par  Hong Kong   16984.44     17200.9