\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore dlr believers tested by trade picture. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sarah Cheung \par \uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2000\par 09:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Feb 25 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar looks set to remain pressured by a weak yen and euro in the near-term, having defied forecasts of a strong rise early in the year. \par \par \uc2  "We still maintain that dollar/yen will go up, and the Sing dollar will follow that," said an analyst at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  "The issue with the yen is not so much a direct impact on the Sing dollar, more that Asia is a major trading bloc," he said, adding that Singapore's major export rivals - Korea and Taiwan - also tended to be influenced by yen weakness. \par \par \uc2  The euro's soft tone was also weighing on the Singapore dollar as Europe is the country's most important non-oil export market after the United States, he said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the authorities seemed fairly relaxed about the Singapore dollar's slide since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out sharp swings in the exchange rate, but they did not sense unease with the Sing dollar's overall trend. \par \par \uc2  "The Singapore dollar is considered a cheap funding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of the low interest rates. But MAS does not want it to become internationalised," an analyst at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  Singapore has gradually liberalised the use of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in equity and debt markets, but the authorities have resisted internationalising it due to the small, open economy. \par \par \uc2  Chartists expected the U.S. dollar to meet resistance at S$1.72, with a second, stronger band at S$1.74. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was at 1.7095 at 0700 GMT. Economic data out this week have been below expectations, knocking the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down to around 1.7150 from 1.7020 late last week. \par \par \uc2  Gross domestic product (GDP) data released on Thursday were at 5.4 percent for 1999, a shade below preliminary numbers of 5.6 percent, but had limited impact on the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  did take a knock from export data, showing a 7.6 percent rise on the year to January compared with December's 25 percent jump. \par \par \uc2  Analysts attributed the poor performance to a supply glitch in the global electronics industry, while the government said it was mainly due to Y2K factors. \par \par \uc2  "The GDP figures were lower than expected, but the disappointing non-oil export figures before that took away most of the bite," an analyst said. \par \par \uc2  "The interesting point to note is that in a survey of manufacturers, they said price competition was the number one obstacle to getting export orders." \par \par \uc2  This added weight to the argument that there would be a more relaxed exchange rate policy, he said. \par \par \uc2  But most analysts maintained their bullish long-term forecasts for the Singapore dollar on expectations of solid growth this year. \par \par \uc2  "The direction over the medium term is still for Singapore dollar strength to 1.50 by year end," said Steve Brice, treasury economist at Standard Chartered. ((Sarah Cheung, Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  desk (65) 970-3841;fax (65) 870-3787; e-mail asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw2p06g0r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\