\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Open Lower; Pressure Seen Sustained \b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2000\par 01:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mostly down against the U.S. dollar as Asian trading hours begin Friday. \par \par \uc2  The pressure on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflects an overnight slide in the Japanese yen and extends the broad market trend prevailing Thursday. \par \par \uc2  At 0015 GMT (7:15 p.m. EST), the U.S. dollar is quoted against the Singapore dollar at S$1.7150, compared with S$1.7134 late in Asia the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Some traders are looking for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade higher still to levels around S$1.7200 in the short term, arguing that with the U.S. dollar strong against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally, the probability that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is small. \par \par \uc2  With few surprises expected in Singapore's 2000 budget, due to be presented today, and the market already pricing in a tighter fiscal stance, dealers expect little impact on the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah, the U.S. dollar is at IDR7,530, up from IDR7,485 late the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Overnight trading saw the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed up to breach resistance above IDR7,500, on heightened concerns over the frail health of Indonesian president Abdurrahman Wahid, who canceled his program of meetings Thursday for a medical examination. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the U.S. dollar is quoted at THB38.175, a touch softer than THB38.190 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  Trading on the Philippine Dealing System is due to open at 0100 GMT. At the close of trading Thursday, the U.S. dollar was at PHP40.870, up sharply from the previous day. \par \par \uc2  In North Asian trading in the won is set to start at 0030 GMT. At Thursday's close the dollar was trading at KRW1,140.50, after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier traded to a six-week high at KRW1,141.00. \par \par \uc2  Domestic dealing in Taipei is scheduled to begin at 0100 GMT. At the end of the last session the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted against the New Taiwan dollar at NT$30.785. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw2p0129s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
