\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Soggy as yen wilts. \b0\par\par\uc2 878 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2000\par 10:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Feb 24 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  retreated in late trade on Thursday as the dollar maintained \par \par \uc2  its toehold around 111 yen. \par \par \uc2      Activity in the spot market was expected to be subdued on \par \par \uc2  Friday as the value date falls on February 29. Dealers said \par \par \uc2  players are cautious of any possible computer glitches as some \par \par \uc2  systems might not recognise a leap year of 2000. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar hovered around 111 yen\tab     after meeting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong resistance above 111.50 from options-related selling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Chartists said dollar/yen looked poised to extend its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par uptrend to the 112.70-113.00 target.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Use a rally of this magnitude to exit longs and as a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par chance to reposition on a two to three days reaction back to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 111 again," said a report by Capital Management.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the dollar appreciated through parity with the euro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   , recouping recent losses after remarks by Federal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan boosted U.S. technology stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won came off in sympathy with the soft yen as offshore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign names and local banks continued to buy dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Exporters, which previously offered at around 1,128, held\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on to the U.S. unit in anticipation of a further rise, adding\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to  downward pressure on the won.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Bank of Korea said on Thursday the current account\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par surplus fell to $25 billion in 1999 from $40.56 billion in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1998. The surplus narrowed as the economic recovery pushed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand for imports, officials said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But on a positive note, Korea's vice minister of commerce\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said he expected a $100 million trade surplus in February\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par following a deficit of $400 million in January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah moved in a narrow 7,400-7,480 range amid thin\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par commercial demand after Jakarta was put on alert for possible\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par protests the previous day, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite some demand from Asian names which lifted the unit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in early trade, the market was generally on the bid for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said dollar/rupiah resistance is seen at 7485 in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the near-term and any break below 7,270 would negate a bullish\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tone.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht retained its soft tone due to a wave of dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying from offshore players.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A baht liquidity squeeze which had been rather severe in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the past few days subsided, easing dollar selling pressure,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers in Singapore said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One European house suggested clients buy the baht in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par swap market at 12 months on dips to discount level 42 for a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par move up to discount level 10.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The next barrier for dollar/baht was seen at 38.40, while\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 37.80 offered solid support as players were expected to buy on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dips at that level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A downgrade in the country's sovereign risk outlook by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thomson Financial BankWatch added to peso woes, pushing it to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its lowest level since early December.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It fell through key support at 40.85 after Thomson changed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its outlook on the Philippines to stable from positive due to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lacklustre economic performance and its large fiscal burden.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market will be shut on Friday for a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par holiday to celebrate the people's power revolution of 1986.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dollar bulls weighed further on the Singapore dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par despite sound economic data released early in the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said gross domestic product growth of 5.4 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the whole of 1999 had met average expectations and that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par upside risk in dollar/yen had dulled sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said players were likely to test dollar/Sing upside to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.72 per dollar, though they would be on guard for signs of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (MAS).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     One dealer from a European bank said the MAS was likely to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par defend the Sing dollar near 1.7210/20.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar ended barely changed after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold U.S. dollars to counteract the negative effects of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tense relations with China.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     China issued a "White paper" on Monday demanding the island\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par enter peace talks or face attack.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taipei dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  defended the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at the T$30.8 level, slowing U.S. dollar demand and keeping\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some players sidelined.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A T$30.75-T$30.8 range was seen for Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0943 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     111.15\tab  110.62\tab    -0.48\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7135\tab  1.7091\tab    -0.26\par  Taiwan dlr     30.79\tab   30.79\tab    +0.02\par  Korean won   1140.00\tab 1135.00\tab    -0.44\par  Baht\tab      38.08\tab   38.03\tab    -0.13\par  Peso\tab      40.88\tab   40.68\tab    -0.49\par  Rupiah\tab  7475.00\tab 7440.00\tab    -0.47\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     111.15\tab  102.21\tab    -8.04\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7135\tab  1.6640\tab    -2.89\par  Taiwan dlr     30.79\tab   31.38\tab    +1.93\par  Korean won   1140.00\tab 1135.00\tab    -0.44\par  Baht\tab      38.08\tab   37.45\tab    -1.65\par  Peso\tab      40.88\tab   40.20\tab    -1.66\par  Rupiah\tab  7475.00\tab 6975.00\tab    -6.69\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7997\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Desk (65) 870-3090\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par email:asia.\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 @reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw2o06oxg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
