\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  risky as rates rise - Merrill. \b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2000\par 08:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Feb 22 (Reuters) - Asian central banks face a growing dilemma as they try to rein in appreciating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a backdrop of gradually rising short-term interest rates, Merrill Lynch said in a research report. \par \par \uc2  The policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to buy dollars and then sterilising the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  - or mopping up the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected into the system - would become increasingly untenable as interest rates headed higher, Merrill's February Asian strategy report said. \par \par \uc2  Growing trade surpluses and capital inflows bolstered Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, prompting central banks to buy an estimated $65 billion in dollars in the spot market. \par \par \uc2  The fact that base money went up only slightly suggested that the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been mostly sterilised, Merrill said. \par \par \uc2  While this policy could continue in a context of low inflation and large external surpluses, it noted that the Bank of Korea's recent decision to raise key overnight rates revealed that inflation was not the only consideration in a monetary tightening. \par \par \uc2  "The BOK stated that there was no inflation threat in sight, but wanted to narrow the spread between short and long rates; it is likely concerned over banks' excessive reliance on short-term credit." \par \par \uc2  Despite the still-benign inflation environment in most of Asia, Merrill said interest rates were set to climb as more central banks used monetary policy to address any banking sector imbalances that might pose risks to macroeconomic stability. \par \par \uc2  And the resulting rate hikes could in turn weigh, given that much of Asia's early asset price recovery was driven by domestic institutions flush with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -infused liquidity. \par \par \uc2  With foreign funds set to continue buying into the Asian recovery, central banks were likely to either step up their \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sterilisation efforts or allow their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen. \par \par \uc2  "Either option would be unwelcome - sterilisation gets more expensive and ineffective as interest rates rise while \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation at a mature stage of recovery has always been a difficult option to pursue," it said. \par \par \uc2  But Merrill added that Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with flexible exchange rate regimes remained greatly undervalued against the dollar despite recovering substantially from their 1998 lows. \par \par \uc2  It said the rupiah and ringgit were 33 percent and 27 percent undervalued respectively, while the Thai baht and Philippine peso were more than 20 percent undervalued. \par \par \uc2  Even the Korean won, whose dramatic gains have drawn frequent official comment and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was nearly 15 percent below its fair value, while the Singapore and Taiwan dollars were some eight and nine percent undervalued. \par \par \uc2  Merrill said its study computed nominal effective exchange rates based on the top 10 trade partners of individual countries in 1999, using the pre-crisis first half of 1997 as a base. \par \par \uc2  It then worked out the real effective exchange rates and used trends in these to derive the fair value of individual \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  ((Sonali Desai, Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3090; Email: sonali.desai@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw2m06up0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
