\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Gains Late On Back Of Euro \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2000\par 10:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar strengthened slightly against the U.S. dollar late Monday as it tracked gains in the euro and the yen. \par \par \uc2  Around 0908 GMT (4:08 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7067, down from S$1.7085 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The market is cooling down after two days of buying pressure" that boosted the U.S. dollar against the Singapore dollar, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar is linked to a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is thought to include the dollar, the euro and yen. \par \par \uc2  Generally, a change in the U.S. dollar against one of the other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  mirrors the U.S. dollar's performance against the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  Late Tuesday, the U.S. dollar gave up ground against the yen, falling to Y111.24 from a peak of Y111.71 early in the day. The euro rose US$0.9990, up from US$0.9873 late Monday in Europe. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the Singapore dollar dropped sharply after the release of figures showing that export growth in January was far lower than expected. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers, however, said the Singapore dollar had been oversold, and that some participants Tuesday were buying back the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  also eased some pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, dealers said. The MAS is said to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth volatility. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 2.1875%, up from 1.500% late Monday. The three-month rate was offered at 2.375%, up from 2.250%. \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw2m00z3o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
