\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Lower Early On Nasdaq Record \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2000\par 01:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are weaker early Friday on U.S. dollar gains after yet another record night on the Nasdaq. \par \par \uc2  The Nasdaq Composite Index jumped 2.8% Thursday to a new all-time high close of 4,485.63. This is the second record in the past three sessions, and it helped push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher against the yen and euro. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is quoted at IDR7,310, up from IDR7,295 late Thursday as traders lock in some profits on long rupiah positions. \par \par \uc2  Positive political and corporate developments, particularly a shakeup in the management of Indonesian automaker Astra in preparation for its sale, helped fuel the rupiah's recent gains from IDR7,700. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar is weaker against its U.S. counterpart. A recent underperformance of local stocks is a factor. The benchmark Straits Times Index is down 10.3% from the end of 1999. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect any further weakness in the Singapore dollar will be limited to S$1.7000. They say the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at that level to curb the slide of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . MAS bought Singapore dollars last week between S$1.7000 and S$1.7100. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is trading at S$1.6950 from S$1.6912 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the U.S. dollar was trading at THB37.425 from THB37.365 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  However, the won may buck the regional weakness and extend Thursday's rise when domestic trade begins at 0030 GMT in Seoul. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea, Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Thursday raised its one-day call rate by 25 basis points to 5%, the first time it has lifted short-term rates since December 1997. Late in the day, the dollar was quoted at KRW1120.5, down from KRW1123.1 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Trade in the New Taiwan dollar and peso will commence at 0100 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ended Taipei trade Thursday at NT$30.613, down from NT$30.665 a day earlier. In Manila it finished at PHP40.385 from PHP40.460. \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw2b00sh6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
