\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Higher Late Ahead Of Lunar New Year \b0\par\par\uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2000\par 09:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are higher in late Asian trading Friday, although a number of markets were closed for a lunar New Year holiday. \par \par \uc2  Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were buoyed by the rupiah, which rose as fears of a military coup arising from a standoff between Indonesian President Abdurrahman Wahid and powerful Security Minister General Wiranto receded. \par \par \uc2  A rise in the local overnight interest rate after authorities decided Thursday to tighten the money supply also helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  There is a growing belief in financial markets that Wiranto will resign from the Cabinet without fuss when Wahid returns to the country on Feb. 13. \par \par \uc2  Traders took heart from comments by Indonesian Defense Minister Juwono Sudarsono, which appeared to indicate Wahid is softening his line on Wiranto and will negotiate a graceful exit for the former military chief. \par \par \uc2  Sudarsono said he passed on to Wiranto a request from Wahid for him to step down immediately, but indicated nothing may happen until the president returns. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is at IDR7,520, down from IDR7,660 late Thursday and a four-month high of IDR7,700 earlier that day. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar rose sharply on the back of the stronger rupiah, a rise in local stock prices, and ongoing fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sold U.S. dollars earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  The Straits Times Index rose 9.6 points, or 0.4%, to 2,258.9. \par \par \uc2  Late in the day, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6870, down from S$1.6955 previously. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the baht rose strongly against the U.S. dollar in line with the stronger Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a higher yen. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the baht may rise further on the back of more corporate restructuring and foreign investment, both of which helped lift Thailand out of a severe recession. \par \par \uc2  Citigroup and IDEAglobal.com economists expect the baht to breach 36.000 against the dollar by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  "The capital account should support the baht. We expect capital inflows," said Citigroup economist Anusorn Tamajai. \par \par \uc2  Still, Anusorn warns the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may come under pressure during that period, especially "when the government and corporates pay external debts." \par \par \uc2  Last September, the dollar rose above THB40 amid a round of corporate foreign-debt repayment. \par \par \uc2  In late trade, the dollar is at THB37.500 down from THB37.680 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The peso also ended the week higher at PHP40.535 to the dollar from PHP40.680 a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won and New Taiwan dollar markets were closed due to holidays in South Korea and Taiwan. The U.S. dollar ended Thursday at KRW1,129.9 and NT$30.775. \par \par \uc2  -By Benjamin Pedley; 65-421-4485;ben.pedley@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw2400pkq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
