\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Higher Early Ahead Of Lunar New Year \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2000\par 02:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are higher against the dollar in early Asian trading Friday, led by a rebound in the rupiah after Indonesian authorities decided to tighten money supply, and thereby push up interest rates. \par \par \uc2  But, a number of regional markets are closed Friday for a lunar New Year holiday. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah is up in early trade after touching a four-month intraday low of 7,700 against the dollar Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said a Bank Indonesia decision to tighten monetary supply, and thereby push up the overnight rate toward 10%, helped the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  There is also a growing belief in the markets that Security Minister Gen. Wiranto will resign or be dismissed from the Cabinet when President Abdurrahman Wahid returns to the country on Feb. 13. \par \par \uc2  This would scuttle talk of a possible military coup, which has weighed on the rupiah for a number of weeks. Wahid demands Wiranto step down after a government report implicated him and other military officials in atrocities last year in the former Indonesian province of East Timor. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is at IDR7,560, down from IDR7,660 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar is up in early trade as dealers are wary of selling at these levels for fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has had an interest to sell U.S. dollars above S$1.7000. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is at S$1.6915, down from S$1.6955 previously, and at 37.580 against the baht, down from THB37.680 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Trade in the peso will start in Manila at 0100 GMT. It ended Thursday at 40.680 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  All other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are closed for the day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended Thursday at KRW1,129.9 and NTD$30.775. \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw2400p19\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
