\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Down Early; IDR Hurt By Political Concerns \b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2000\par 01:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are lower against the U.S. dollar early Wednesday as another strong night on Wall Street helped the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a four-month high against the yen, and a new all-time high against the euro. \par \par \uc2  In addition, political concerns are weighing on the rupiah as a showdown between Indonesian President Abdurrahman Wahid and Security Minister General Wiranto looms. \par \par \uc2  Wahid, who was in London overnight for meetings with the U.K. government, again called for Wiranto to quit his Cabinet post after a government report blamed him and other top officers for atrocities in East Timor last year. \par \par \uc2  Wiranto has declined to respond to calls for him to resign, which some observers interpret as a sign he will seek to remain in the Cabinet. \par \par \uc2  This would add to tension between the administration and disgruntled elements of the military, and likely spark renewed talk of a possible military coup, although Wahid dismissed such speculation as "hogwash." \par \par \uc2  However, there should be some good news for the Indonesian economy and rupiah later Wednesday. The Consultative Group for Indonesia, which comprises the main foreign donors to Indonesia, is expected to pledge around $4.5 billion in new loans to Jakarta to help it finance its budget. The CGI is holding its annual meeting Tuesday and Wednesday in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  In early Asian trade, the dollar was quoted at 7,470 rupiah, up slightly from IDR7,450 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar is weaker against its U.S. counterpart, weighed down by the rupiah and proposed foreign acquisitions by local companies such as Singapore Airlines S$1.6 billion buy of a 49% stake in Virgin Atlantic. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expect the U.S. dollar will test above S$1.7000. \par \par \uc2  "The market wants to see if the MAS will step in to buy Singapore dollars as they did on Monday at S$1.7100," said a U.S. bank trader. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Monday to slow the steep decline of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted against the Singapore dollar at S$1.6985, up from S$1.6955 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  The won opened weaker in Seoul at 1,129.0 against the dollar from KRW1,126.6 at Tuesday's close, with traders citing dollar buying by state banks. The dollar ended higher Tuesday on buying by the state-run Korea Development Bank and net selling of local stocks by foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at 37.515 Thai baht, up slightly from THB37.505 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Domestic trade in Taipei and Manila is scheduled to commence at 0100 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar edged higher Tuesday to close at NT$30.681 against the U.S. dollar from NT$30.699 a day earlier, while the peso ended Tuesday at 40.550 pesos from PHP40.572 at Monday's. \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw2200kia\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
