\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Falls To 4-Mo Low Late On Corp US$ Orders \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2000\par 09:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar plunged to a four-month low against the U.S. dollar late Friday on aggressive U.S. dollar buying by DBS Bank on behalf of corporate customers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At about 0830 GMT (3:30 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7023, up from S$1.6892 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  DBS Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers were unavailable for comment, but a dealer at a U.S. bank estimated that DBS bought US$1 billion in the market. \par \par \uc2  Traders said DBS could be buying on behalf of Singapore Airlines Ltd., which recently announced it was taking a stake in Virgin Airways, or Singapore Telecommunications Ltd., which is in merger talks with Cable & Wireless HKT. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.S. bank said the Singapore dollar is almost certainly trading outside its accepted trade-weighted band, and he expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore to step into the market to prop up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I'm a little surprised they haven't been in yet," he said. \par \par \uc2  Such a move would be highly unusual for the MAS since it usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets by selling \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars in a bid to preserve export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the U.S. dollar will probably retreat next week, especially as players square their positions on the last day of the month on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 1.875%, up from 1.750% late Thursday. The three-month rate was offered at 2.3125%, down from 2.4375%. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807; anita.jain@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw1s00lqt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
