\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Ends Unchanged, But Up From Intraday Lows \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2000\par 09:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar bounced back from intraday lows to end virtually unchanged late Thursday as institutions locked in gains from long U.S. dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  At about 0810 GMT (3:10 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6892, compared with S$1.6891 late Wednesday. Early Thursday, the dollar hit an intraday high of S$1.6933. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said U.S. and Hong-Kong based institutions liquidated long U.S. dollar positions at the level of about S$1.6930, lifting the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In addition, dealers said, local banks sold the U.S. dollar on behalf of commercial clients, sparking rumors of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The MAS generally works through local banks when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. However, the rumor was met with some skepticism, since the MAS is said to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, rather than strengthen it. \par \par \uc2  Investors sold the U.S. dollar as it approached its long-term resistance level of S$1.7000. That level should remain an effective cap on the U.S. dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, political uncertainty in Indonesia and the prospect of an interest rate hike in the U.S. when the Federal Open Market Committee meets next month will limit the downside for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Thursday's dealing also saw unwinding of long Thai baht positions against the Singapore dollar. Some players had sold Singapore dollars for baht to take advantage of relatively higher interest rates in Thailand. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 1.750%, down from 1.875% late Wednesday. The three-month rate was offered unchanged at 2.4375%. \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw1r00jtg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
