\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Retreat on G7, choppy session seen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,124 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2000\par 03:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 24 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  were mostly lower in early trade on Monday in a knee jerk \par \par \uc2  reaction to the Group of Seven nations' weekend statement that \par \par \uc2  they share Japan's concerns about the strong yen. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said they expected trade to be choppy in the run up \par \par \uc2  to the Federal Reserve's policy meeting on February 1 and 2. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen\tab     gained ground after retreating against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par greenback in early Tokyo trade as buyers squared long positions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in disappointment over the dollar's failure to sustain a rally.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Over the longer-term, the yen is seen supported by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreigners' investment in Tokyo stocks and buying by Japanese\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exporters, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "There was some dollar buying in early trade. But I don't\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par think the dollar's rise would be sustained. There was no pledge\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of possible coordinated action to check the yen's rise, only\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sympathy," said a dealer at a major European bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some dealers said recent losses in the Dow Jones index\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could put the dollar on firmer footing against the regionals in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the near-term as it could mean lower foreign inflows into local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah pierced the 7,300 level as further fighting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between Christians and Moslems in the spice islands broke out\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over the weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Fundamentally, the rupiah should not be this bad because\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the upward trend since end-December has not been threatened," a\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was also unrest on the island resort of Bintan, near\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore, where Indonesian police and military forces\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dispersed demonstrators, injuring 13 people.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The analyst noted that the protests in Bintan for the past\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week were over land rights claims by villagers and were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par isolated from religious riots in the rest of the country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, he said dollar/rupiah could head for 7,400, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reasonable support seen at 7,250.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Finance Minister Bambang Sudibyo was quoted by local press\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over the weekend as saying the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did not need to be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recapitalised after all.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Sudibyo was quoted by the Jakarta Post as saying an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par accounting adjustment showed Bank Indonesia actually had 100\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trillion rupiah in assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won was lower against the dollar as banks, which had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bought dollars believing the won might be hurt by news of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par merchant bank's suspension, reversed course as market sentiment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appeared little changed, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Friday, the Financial Supervisory Commission ordered\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nara Investment Banking Corp , which had been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par staggering due to its large exposure to the ailing Daewoo Group\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par , to halt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for three months from on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Saturday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A local bank dealer said market players bought dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after the news but the impact was shortlived.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Underlying market sentiment was still betting on the won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strengthening as foreign investors kept up their interest in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par direct and equity investment in Korea, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the market was also cautious about dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par holdings as they believed the authorities would continue to\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent volatility.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Local bank buying of U.S. dollars and technical factors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weighed on the Sing dollar while a clash between police and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par protesters on the neighbouring Indonesian island of Bintan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unsettled sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chartists said dollar/Sing was well entrenched in an upward\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par channel from Jan 4 and that 1.6850 was seen as a strong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resistance level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If touched, the U.S. dollar was likely to slip as the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par channel looked a little over-extended. Support was seen at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1.6775/80.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One analyst said local banks had been seen supporting the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollar again with a view to keeping it between the 1.67\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and 1.69 level in the medium term, to keep exports competitive.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Developments on Bintan, where Singapore has investments,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were keeping players slightly wary though there seemed to be no\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par real effect on flows as yet, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht edged down on importer dollar demand. The unit is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to move in a narrow range in the near-term due to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par modest commercial demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rating agency Fitch IBCA says Thai commercial banks appear\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on track to return to profitability this year, but some -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par including top banks like Bangkok Bank  and Siam\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Commercial Bank  - are likely to need to make further\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par provisions against loan losses.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some analysts said the worst was over for Thai banks after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they reported massive losses for 1999 last week, blaming the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par poor results on huge loan losses provisionings.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso tracked the baht lower due to commercial demand\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the U.S. dollar, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market showed little immediate reaction to positive\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par January-October current account data released on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the Philippines posted a hefty\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par current account surplus of $5.55 billion in the first ten\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par months of 1999, exceeding the full-year target of $1.67\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It also cut its overnight lending rate to 11 percent from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 12 percent. The bank had raised its lending rate to 12 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par last month when it opened a facility to meet banks' immediate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cash requirements for the Y2K cross over.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar was slightly firmer and well within the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par parameters of a recent range carved out by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The firmer yen and expected inflows by foreign equity funds\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were expected to drive gains in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was expected to cap any significant upside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par December unemployment figures were expected at 0300 GMT but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a local newspaper quoted the Statistics Office as saying the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par jobless rate stood at an expected 2.85 percent in December and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par an all-time record high of 2.92 percent for all of 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0215 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     104.80\tab  104.90\tab    +0.10\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6837\tab  1.6746\tab    -0.54\par  Taiwan dlr     30.75\tab   30.78\tab    +0.10\par  Korean won   1126.80\tab 1128.00\tab    +0.11\par  Baht\tab      37.26\tab   37.23\tab    -0.08\par  Peso\tab      40.67\tab   40.60\tab    -0.17\par  Rupiah\tab  7305.00\tab 7285.00\tab    -0.27\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     104.80\tab  102.21\tab    -2.47\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6837\tab  1.6640\tab    -1.17\par  Taiwan dlr     30.75\tab   31.38\tab    +2.05\par  Korean won   1126.80\tab 1135.00\tab    +0.73\par  Baht\tab      37.26\tab   37.45\tab    +0.51\par  Peso\tab      40.67\tab   40.20\tab    -1.16\par  Rupiah\tab  7305.00\tab 6975.00\tab    -4.52\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7997\tab    -0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Desk (65) 870-3087\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par email:asia.\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 @reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw1o022in\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
