\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Boosted as U.S. inflation fears fade. \b0\par\par\uc2 933 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2000\par 03:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 17 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly \par \par \uc2  firmer in early Monday trade after more evidence that U.S. \par \par \uc2  inflation was looking tame pushed the Dow to yet another record \par \par \uc2  closing high. \par \par \uc2      That was seen as giving regional stocks and sentiment in \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  a boost. \par \par \uc2      Eagerly awaited Consumer Price Index data for December came \par \par \uc2  in at a less than anticipated 0.2 percent, compared to \par \par \uc2  expectations for an average 0.3 percent increase according to a \par \par \uc2  recent Reuters poll. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that had underpinned hopes the U.S. Federal \par \par \uc2  Reserve might stop at a 25 basis point rise when it meets on \par \par \uc2  February 1 and 2. \par \par \uc2  Wall Street's fortunes pushed the dollar to its highest \par \par \uc2  levels against the euro in 1-weeks on Friday but failed to \par \par \uc2  have any visible impact on dollar/yen which sagged. \par \par \uc2  By early Asia, dollar/yen was a shade easier on sporadic \par \par \uc2  selling by U.S. operators but its downside was seen supported \par \par \uc2  near 105.50 yen. \par \par \uc2      The euro remained pressured but was off lows seen on Friday \par \par \uc2  while follow-through sales also weighed on euro/yen. \par \par \uc2      U.S. markets are closed Monday a partial market and public \par \par \uc2  holiday for Martin Luther King day. The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \par \par \uc2  remains open. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won was bid at its highest level since late 1997 early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as players sold dollars offshore and the market remained\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positive over a pre-weekend cabinet re-shuffle.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Although firmer, a weekly chart showed the pair was only\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par just out of its recent range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Newly appointed finance minister Lee Hun-jai had been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quoted by a ministry official as saying he favoured a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market driven more by market forces.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The status of the country's current account also gave\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment a boost, with the government expecting it to reach\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $26 billion in 1999, topping a target of $20 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The finance ministry said at the weekend that exports rose\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nine percent to $144.2 billion year-on-year in 1999 while\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par imports climbed 28.3 percent to $119.7 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The ministry also said it wanted to stabilise long-term\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rates in the light of imminent redemptions at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investment trusts and consumer prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bullishness over domestic stocks kept the baht buoyed, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers expecting capital to continue flowing into the country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Bangkok said the market had already factored in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a 25 basis point U.S. rate hike by the Fed in February.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Thailand based analysts said domestic stocks could climb\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between 25 to 35 percent in 2000 after advancing some 35\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso strengthened, with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par indicating that interest rates could still head lower.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said on Friday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par there was still room to lower overnight rates despite an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected U.S. rate hike.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He said low domestic inflation would give the bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par flexibility to cut rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Monetary Board decided on Friday to keep its overnight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates -- 12 percent for lending and 8.75 percent for borrowing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -- unchanged for next week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar was slightly firmer, with dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expecting foreign funds to persist as net buyers of domestic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign funds bought up T$4.559 billion worth of domestic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks on Friday, racking up a total T$24.625 billion (US$798\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million) over five straight sessions of net buying.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers said they expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to remain\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ever-vigilant over any sharp moves higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The bank had capped it at around the T$30.84 level on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Saturday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar is likely to continue to be driven by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity market this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     With the Dow closing on Friday at its third record high\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par last week, dealers expected the local stock market and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par subsequently the Sing dollar to be well-supported, .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But 1.6550 was expected to be a strong barrier for the Sing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the near term as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to by U.S. dollars at that level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah nudged up against the dollar on the back of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par firming regionals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said a major Singaporean name was in the market to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buy a sizeable amount of the rupe in early.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The sentiment was buoyed by President Abdurrahman Wahid's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong remarks that he would deal sternly with "provocateurs"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par he blamed for stirring violence in the Moluccas and separatist\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tension in restive Aceh province.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But 7,000 remained a strong barrier in the near-term.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0139 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest b