\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Weaker, eyeing Wall Street. \b0\par\par\uc2 801 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2000\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 14 (Reuters) - Most Asian regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were softer late on Friday as players adjusted \par \par \uc2  positions, awaiting Wall Street's reaction to remarks by \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve chief Alan Greenspan. \par \par \uc2      Greenspan told the Economic Club of New York late on \par \par \uc2  Thursday that the Fed is intent on defusing mounting imbalances \par \par \uc2  between supply and demand, and will support higher borrowing \par \par \uc2  costs to take some heat out of the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2   The market was divided, with some dealers expecting U.S. \par \par \uc2  financial markets to take Greenspan's comments in stride as \par \par \uc2  they confirmed an already discounted 25-basis-point rate hike. \par \par \uc2      "But there are others who think the remarks might signal \par \par \uc2  the possibilities of the Fed opting for a 50 basis point rate \par \par \uc2  hike in February rather than 25 as earlier expected," said a \par \par \uc2  dealer at a U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      "This led to some profit taking and position adjustments \par \par \uc2  ahead of the weekend. That said, there were no drastic moves in \par \par \uc2  the market. Trade is normally thin on Friday," he said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won bucked the trend, rising on the new finance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par minister's market-friendly comments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Finance Minister Lee Hun-jai on Friday stressed the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par importance of market forces in restructuring the corporate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sector. He also said the government would shun \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market unless it was volatile.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But further upside for the won could be limited given that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar is edging toward oversold territory against the won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the 14-day relative strength index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah wilted against the dollar, with 7,300 seen as a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par solid support near-term but dealers said 7,100 could be a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong resistance for now as investors are expected to buy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars near that level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Sentiment was dampened by tensions between Moslems and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Christians in the spice islands.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indonesia's military said on Friday it would send hundreds\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of crack troops to the islands to quell widespread violence.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was wedged in a narrow range in listless trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy making Monetary Board\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decided to keep overnight rates steady next week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said so long as the peso does not weaken beyond 41\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar, Philippine authorities should be able to keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rates low, at least until the next U.S. Federal Open\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market Committee meeting on February 1 and 2.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar edged lower after the stock market failed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to sustain its recent momentum.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Recent aggressive dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had pressured investors to slow down their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par greenback selling, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The demand for the local unit also dwindled as investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par retreated from the market to await Wall Street's reaction to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the hawkish remarks made by Greenspan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar slipped during the Asian session,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reflecting the stock market's slide, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The downside could be limited as the US dollar is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par approaching overbought territory on the 14-day relative\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strength index with a reading of 67.514.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But 1.6550 was expected to be a strong barrier for the Sing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the near term as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy U.S. dollars at that level, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht edged lower, with some dealers recommending their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par clients trade it in a range of 37.30 to 37.55 against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SEB Merchant Banking said if the pair broke above 37.55\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par convincingly, the next resistance for the dollar would be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 37.80.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One analyst said any fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par curb the baht had been allayed by the baht's weaker tone after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Deputy Prime Minister Supachai Panitchpakdi said a strong\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could hurt Thailand's trade surplus.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0746 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     105.69\tab  105.69\tab    +0.00\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6724\tab  1.6665\tab    -0.35\par  Taiwan dlr     30.82\tab   30.73\tab    -0.29\par  Korean won   1124.50\tab 1135.00\tab    +0.93\par  Baht\tab      37.47\tab   37.45\tab    -0.05\par  Peso\tab      40.58\tab   40.59\tab    +0.02\par  Rupiah\tab  7200.00\tab 7175.00\tab    -0.35\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     105.69\tab  102.21\tab    -3.29\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6724\tab  1.6640\tab    -0.50\par  Taiwan dlr     30.82\tab   31.38\tab    +1.82\par  Korean won   1124.50\tab 1135.00\tab    +0.93\par  Baht\tab      37.47\tab   37.45\tab    -0.05\par  Peso\tab      40.58\tab   40.20\tab    -0.94\par  Rupiah\tab  7200.00\tab 6975.00\tab    -3.13\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7997\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 