\par\par \b \uc2  POLL - Asia  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  seen strengthening in 2000. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 1,253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2000\par 01:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 14 (Reuters) - Robust global growth and a \par \par \uc2  gradual pick-up in inflationary pressures should see most Asian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  reaching for higher ground this year. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters poll of 92 economists and dealers across Asia \par \par \uc2  found that regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are set to ride a wave of \par \par \uc2  investment and asset inflows, leaving the worst of the crisis \par \par \uc2  far behind. \par \par \uc2  As inflation picks up alongside rising imports, employment \par \par \uc2  and consumer demand in the second half, central banks are \par \par \uc2  expected to allow their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  more leeway to appreciate. \par \par \uc2  "The authorities may be approaching a policy crossroad in \par \par \uc2  managing the current economic cycle," said Chia-Liang Lian, \par \par \uc2  fixed income stategist at Merrill Lynch. \par \par \uc2  "Specifically, central banks could acquiesce to stronger \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  if balance of payments inflows continue unabated \par \par \uc2  amid maturing economic recoveries," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Australian and New Zealand dollars are expected to make \par \par \uc2  strong headway thanks to rising commodity prices, while the \par \par \uc2  Korean won, which gained 5.4 percent in 1999, is seen surging \par \par \uc2  some 10 percent by the end of 2000. \par \par \uc2  Marginal gains are predicted for the Thai baht and \par \par \uc2  Philippine peso, which lost about three percent each against \par \par \uc2  the dollar last year amid worries about public and private \par \par \uc2  sector debt. \par \par \uc2  As much of the upside for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to \par \par \uc2  be driven by foreign portfolio flows, analysts warn that any \par \par \uc2  rout on Wall Street could shake confidence in markets across \par \par \uc2  the Pacific. \par \par \uc2  AUSTRALIAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Higher commodity prices, driven by a pick-up in world \par \par \uc2  growth, are expected to propel the Australian dollar to levels \par \par \uc2  not seen since November 1997. \par \par \uc2  Analysts see the Aussie gaining over five percent to end \par \par \uc2  the year at US$0.7023 against the current US$0.6660, supported \par \par \uc2  by an expected rise in official interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Tax reforms encouraging investment which start in July and \par \par \uc2  the Olympic Games in September should keep the Aussie supported \par \par \uc2  in the second half, but its rise could be slowed by a large \par \par \uc2  trade deficit, yen strength or if commodity prices fail to \par \par \uc2  rally. \par \par \uc2  NEW ZEALAND DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The region's other commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the New Zealand \par \par \uc2  dollar, looks set to soar this year, with analysts predicting \par \par \uc2  an average five percent rise in the first half and a near 10 \par \par \uc2  percent gain over the course of the year. \par \par \uc2  The kiwi lost about 0.5 percent against the U.S. dollar in \par \par \uc2  1999, but analysts said its prospects should improve with the \par \par \uc2  economy now on the verge of sustainable expansion. \par \par \uc2  Expectations of a series of interest rate hikes this year \par \par \uc2  could also bolster the kiwi, but New Zealand's large current \par \par \uc2  account deficit remained a worry, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON \par \par \uc2  Official forecasts of growth in excess of seven percent \par \par \uc2  this year and robust foreign direct and equity investment \par \par \uc2  should help the won extend its blistering rally. \par \par \uc2  Interbank dealers and economists expected the won to gain \par \par \uc2  over five percent by the end of June and some 10 percent by \par \par \uc2  end-2000, from about 1,135 currently. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the won was undervalued due to heavy \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Korean authorities, who are anxious to keep \par \par \uc2  exports competitive, but the government is likely to relax its \par \par \uc2  grip on the exchange rate to curb inflationary pressures. \par \par \uc2  Only a worsening of Daewoo's debt crisis could pose a \par \par \uc2  serious threat to the won uptrend, if it spurred an exodus from \par \par \uc2  Korean asset markets, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Singapore's sound fundamentals and signs of a pick-up in \par \par \uc2  inflation should see the local dollar appreciate steadily \par \par \uc2  through the year, with analysts predicting a five percent gain \par \par \uc2  from the current 1.67 per U.S. dollar by year end. \par \par \uc2  Most houses did not foresee a significant build-up in \par \par \uc2  domestic price pressures but some cautioned that the island \par \par \uc2  remained highly vulnerable to external shocks like a dramatic \par \par \uc2  rise in oil or commodity prices. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \par \par \uc2  recent months to cap the Sing dollar, which is managed against \par \par \uc2  an undisclosed trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But Prime Minister Goh Chok Tong was quoted as saying the \par \par \uc2  island had never depended on a weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stay \par \par \uc2  competitive. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's return to pre-crisis growth rates and a seemingly \par \par \uc2  unstoppable stock market are expected to lift the tightly \par \par \uc2  controlled Taiwan $1.2 percent to 30.36 by year-end. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expected its rise to be muted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- part of an unspoken policy of \par \par \uc2  protecting exporters. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's expected entry to the World Trade Organisation in \par \par \uc2  the second half could see the local dollar benefit from foreign \par \par \uc2  investment flows, though some analysts expected a shrinking \par \par \uc2  trade surplus to weigh on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso should strengthen marginally this year, thanks to \par \par \uc2  strong growth in exports, remittances from Filipinos working \par \par \uc2  overseas and U.S. dollar loan proceeds. \par \par \uc2  But worries about the ballooning budget deficit and growing \par \par \uc2  political risk could limit foreign investment flows. \par \par \uc2  "Although the current account will be very strong, I think \par \par \uc2  because of the domestic political uncertainty with regards to \par \par \uc2  liberalisation and charter change, the Philippines will not \par \par \uc2  outshine the rest of the region," said Chan Chia Lin, head of \par \par \uc2  Asian economic research at ABN Amro Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht is expected to move in a stable range near its \par \par \uc2  current level, supported by a pick-up in capital inflows as \par \par \uc2  Thailand's economic outlook improves. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Thailand could make further headway in \par \par \uc2  repaying foreign debt in the first half, while foreign \par \par \uc2  portfolio flows were likely to improve further into the year. \par \par \uc2  They expected the baht to remain on the weaker side of 37 \par \par \uc2  per dollar on average, but strengthen slightly from its 37.52 \par \par \uc2  level at the end of 1999. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's huge debt overhang and the uncertain fate of \par \par \uc2  President Abdurrahman Wahid's infant government will keep the \par \par \uc2  rupiah a risky buy this year. \par \par \uc2  An improved economic picture is likely to be offset by a \par \par \uc2  jump in imports and foreign debt repayment, as well as worries \par \par \uc2  about communal violence. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect the rupiah to be near current levels by \par \par \uc2  mid-year, with an average forecast of an over seven percent \par \par \uc2  rise to 6,685 per dollar by end-December. \par \par \uc2  MALAYSIAN RINGGIT Malaysia is not expected to abandon its \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg of 3.80 ringgit to the U.S. dollar before June, \par \par \uc2  but half of the research houses polled saw the government \par \par \uc2  re-examining its exchange rate policy beyond mid-2000. \par \par \uc2  This could result in an adjustment of the fixed rate or a \par \par \uc2  move to a managed float, with the undervalued ringgit seen \par \par \uc2  appreciating by about 3.8 percent to 3.66 per dollar by \par \par \uc2  year-end. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad has said the ringgit peg \par \par \uc2  will remain until there is a global agreement on a new \par \par \uc2  financial framework that would prevent speculative attacks on \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab \tab   Rate at 0820 GMT    end-June\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par end-2000\par \f28 \par \par 