\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore MAS Seen Smoothing  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Volatility \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christopher Wellisz \par \uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2000\par 11:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- Recent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar has been aimed at smoothing volatility and discouraging speculation rather than influencing the exchange rate, analysts said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Wednesday to buy U.S. dollars for \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars, said traders, who pointed out the move marked the second time this week the MAS has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  But the MAS action puzzled some observers because it came at a time when the Singapore dollar was falling against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - a trend that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should have welcomed. In the past, the MAS has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to subdue a strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  "From the fundamental point of view there is no compelling reason to tinker with the exchange rate," said Friedrich Wu, chief economist at Development Bank of Singapore. "They are fairly comfortable at this level of S$1.6600 to S$1.6700" to the U.S. dollar, he said. \par \par \uc2  In the absence of reasons to influence the exchange rate, observers said, the MAS was most likely acting to prevent sharp moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "It might just be smoothing fluctuations in the market given that dollar-Sing has been a bit choppy of late," said Thio Chin Loo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banque Paribas in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Other participants added that Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been trying to discourage what it considers to be undue speculation in the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The authority frowns on offshore use of the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for purposes not related to trade or direct investment. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  During London Hours When Trade Is Thin\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Late Wednesday, during London trading hours, traders said the\par authority bought U.S. dollars in several transactions between S$1.6650\par and S$1.6690.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The authority, which generally acts through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  banks,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during London hours when liquidity is thin and the exchange\par rate more volatile, they added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Monday, the MAS bought U.S. dollars at the level of S$1.6600,\par dealers said, at a time when the Singapore dollar and other Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were already weakening in response to declines in local stock\par markets. The MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  accelerated the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar's\par downward move.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MAS spokesman Toh Yong Chuan declined to comment on Thursday, saying\par the authority generally doesn't discuss reports of market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The MAS doesn't target a specific U.S. dollar exchange rate for the\par Singapore dollar. Instead, it guides the Singapore dollar against a\par basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the island-state's most important trading partners.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although the MAS doesn't reveal the structure of the basket, the U.S.\par dollar is thought to represent about 20%, with the yen close behind at\par about 16%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Generally, the MAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to subdue the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar if the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's gains against the U.S. dollar aren't offset by declines\par against the yen or other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the basket, analysts say.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The MAS uses the Singapore dollar exchange rate in order to juggle two\par policy objectives.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the one hand, it wants to keep the exchange rate competitive in\par order to promote economic growth. On the other, it's wary of an overly\par weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that would fuel inflation in the form of higher prices for\par imported goods.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But with exports rising and economy growing at a healthy clip, there's\par no particular need to weaken the Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . If anything,\par analysts say, a mild upturn in inflation suggests that the authority\par will allow the local dollar to strengthen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Christopher Wellisz; 65/ 421-4802;\par christopher.wellisz@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1135 4204 55127 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw1d005vz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
