\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Stabilize; Market Retains Bullish Outlook \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 775 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2000\par 09:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilized late Friday, after suffering sharp falls for two consecutive days, raising hopes that the sell-off that soured trading in the first week of the new year may have played itself out. \par \par \uc2  Although the Singapore dollar ended Asian dealing hours a touch lower, the Thai baht inched upward and the South Korean won and the Philippine peso closed appreciably higher. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is close to topping out against a lot of the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Even on a short term outlook, we're fairly bullish," said Steve Brice, a treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Other analysts backed this view, saying the sell-off in Asian stock markets responsible for propelling the slide in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared close to an end. \par \par \uc2  "The short term jitters which originally caused the equity market correction have been sufficiently priced in," said Vincent Low, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rate strategist at Merrill Lynch in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "Once equity markets are on a firmer footing, the turnaround story will continue and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will resume strengthening," he concluded. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers fretted that even if regional stock prices do level out and recover over the coming week, renewed weakness in the Japanese yen ahead of next weekend's G8 summit meeting in Japan could drag Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower. \par \par \uc2  Brice at Standard Chartered dismissed the fears, however. \par \par \uc2  "The time is long past that the yen's movements were a huge influence on regional market sentiment," he said. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, dealers suspected that with the yen heading lower, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be prepared to covertly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to suppress any \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar appreciation, maintaining the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade-weighted valuation. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the authorities would be too happy to see the Singapore dollar strengthen," said one trader at a foreign bank in the city. "We are seeing strong (U.S. dollar) bids at S$1.6620 from local banks now. I don't think the (U.S.) dollar will go below S$1.6600. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asian dealing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at S$1.6621, well below its earlier intraday high of S$1.6672, but still above S$1.6615 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Among other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Thai baht edged a touch higher, with the U.S. dollar easing to THB37.3750 late in Asian trade from THB37.3950 the previous day. Traders said that solid offers at THB37.7000 should cap any dollar advances in the near term. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won also closed higher after recovering from a sharp early fall that drove the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its lowest level in over a month. \par \par \uc2  An early rash of dollar-buying propelled the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  upward to touch an intraday high of KRW1,156.00, its highest since the first week of December. \par \par \uc2  The dollar soon fell back on profit-taking, however, after Minister of Finance Kang Bong-kyun reiterated the country's high growth and low inflation outlook for 2000 while reassuring markets that the Seoul government has no intention of raising interest rates in the foreseeable future. \par \par \uc2  By the close the dollar had dropped to KRW1,138.00, down from KRW1,146.50 the day before. \par \par \uc2  In other markets, the Philippine peso closed higher after as market volatility eased following the surprise resignation Wednesday of Finance Secretary Edgardo Espiritu. \par \par \uc2  Although uncertainties remained ahead of the appointment during the weekend of a new economic coordinating council, market participants took a broadly positive view of the naming of Trade Secretary Jose Pardo as Espiritu's replacement. \par \par \uc2  By the close, the dollar had fallen back to PHP40.330, from PHP40.550 at the end of Thursday's session. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar closed lower, but dealers attributed the fall to sustained U.S. dollar-buying by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than to negative investor sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Against the Taiwanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. dollar ended at NT$30.860, up from NT$30.854 the previous day. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah also ended the day down. With local markets in Jakarta closed Friday and Monday for the Eid al Fitr religious festival, offshore dealing was thin. Concerns over political developments in Indonesia supported the U.S. dollar, which ended Asian hours at IDR7,175, up from IDR7,165 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com SUBSCRIBERS CAN FIND ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  COMMENT ON: \par \par \uc2  TELERATE PAGES [1136] OR [4250] \par \par \uc2  DOW JONES NEWSWIRES BY SEARCHING THE CODE N/FXW \par \par \uc2  BLOOMBERG BY ENTERING NI FRX \par \par \uc2  REUTERS BY ENTERING CODE \b \highlight22\uc2 