\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Flat Early; Seen Trading In Narrow Range \b0\par\par\uc2 194 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2000\par 03:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar is flat against the U.S. dollar early Thursday and is expected to trade in a narrow range as Asian equities markets stabilize. \par \par \uc2  About 0217 GMT (9:17 p.m. Wednesday EST), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6567, unchanged from late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's recovery in U.S. stocks, which boosted Asian markets early Thursday, is positive for the Singapore dollar and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, concerns that local markets will remain vulnerable to a possible downdraft in the U.S. are keeping investors cautious, they added. \par \par \uc2  Despite the bullish outlook for the Singapore economy, "people aren't really comfortable going short" U.S. dollars, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Expectations of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep the U.S. dollar supported above the level of S$1.6530, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, international merchant banks are selling the U.S. dollar against the Singapore dollar at S$1.6585, a dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  -By Christopher Wellisz; 65/ 421-4802; christopher.wellisz@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw160022w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
