\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Soggy as stocks slide. \b0\par\par\uc2 904 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2000\par 10:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 5 (Reuters) - Hefty losses on Asian stock \par \par \uc2  markets in the wake of Wall Street's slump dented regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, with the recent star performers -- the \par \par \uc2  Korean won, Thai baht and Taiwan dollar -- among the worst hit. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said it was too early to view the declines on \par \par \uc2  Asian bourses as anything more than profit-taking after recent \par \par \uc2  heady gains, but investors were likely to keep a close eye on \par \par \uc2  movements on the Dow Jones index and the high-tech Nasdaq. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen\tab     was pressured in late Asian trade as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par euro/yen reached new six-week highs amid growing bullishness\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about the single European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro\tab     reached new seven-week highs after piercing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a strong barrier around $1.0340-50.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht was dragged off its recent six-month highs as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par major European and U.S. names bought the dollar to settle\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mismatched forward contracts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A near-six percent drop on the SETI and corporate dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand also weighed on the baht, but dealers expected exporter\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar offers to limit its downside to 37.30.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar was depressed alongside its regional\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par counterparts and on the back of a near-six percent drop on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Straits Time share index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers cited rumours that the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the market on Tuesday, buying U.S. dollars around the 1.65\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level to slow the Sing dollar's recent rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official declined comment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rumours. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traditionally\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par says it \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to smooth sharp moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Trade and Industry Minister George Yeo said recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fluctuations in the Sing dollar were due to "normal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par volatility".\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's upside could be limited for now\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as players would remain wary of the MAS, but most expect it to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise in the months ahead as inflation picks up in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won ran into a brick wall as the Kospi suffered its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par biggest ever one-day drop, spurring offshore dollar buying and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-covering by banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors sold a net 112.8 billion won worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Finance Minister Kang Bong-kyun said GDP growth this year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par might exceed seven percent -- compared with a previous forecast\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of five to six percent -- if external conditions improve.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He also said the government would not expand money supply\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of the April general elections.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves to temper a rapid rise in the Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar helped pull it around 0.5 percent lower despite the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local stock market's bravado in the face of losses elsewhere.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The TAIEX\tab      was the only regional bourse to rack up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains after Wall Street's falls overnight, in stark contrast to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par declines of more than five percent in many key markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was expected to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stop the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  firming above the T$30.00 per dollar level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Consumer price index data for the year to December came in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower than expected, at 0.14 percent. Analysts surveyed in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent Reuters poll had forecast an average rise of 0.72\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That put full-year inflation for 1999 at just 0.18 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - its lowest level since 1986 and far below forecasts made a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year ago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso shed nearly one percent as the baht hovered around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 37 per dollar level and as corporate demand for dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par picked up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders in Manila said they expected the peso to remain\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par below 40 per dollar during the year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Inflation remained tame in December, with consumer prices\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rising only 4.3 percent year-on-year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The monthly inflation rate for 1999 hit an average 6.6\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent, with the government saying the monthly rate should\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par average 6-7 percent in 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Jitters over the financial health of the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Bank Indonesia, lingered in what traders described as a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still thin market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah lost more than one and a half percent but was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still trading the right side of 7,200 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A recent audit into the bank suggested its financial\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par position was so problematic it might need to be recapitalised.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Finance Minister Bambang Sudibyo has said the government\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par might issue bonds to recapitalise it and that it may sell some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of them overseas.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0909 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     103.44\tab  102.90\tab    -0.52\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6562\tab  1.6510\tab    -0.31\par  Taiwan dlr     30.73\tab   30.57\tab    -0.52\par  Korean won   1134.00\tab 1121.00\tab    -1.15\par  Baht\tab      37.20\tab   36.80\tab    -1.08\par  Peso\tab      40.15\tab   39.74\tab    -1.02\par  Rupiah\tab  7150.00\tab 7030.00\tab    -1.68\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     103.44\tab  102.21\tab    -1.19\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6562\tab  1.6640\tab    +0.47\par  Taiwan dlr     30.73\tab   31.38\tab    +2.12\par  Korean won   1134.00\tab 1135.00\tab    +0.09\par  Baht\tab      37.20\tab   37.45\tab    +0.67\par  Peso\tab      40.15\tab   40.20\tab    +0.12\par  Rupiah\tab  7150.00\tab 6975.00\tab    -2.45\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7997\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Desk (65) 870-3087\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par email:asia.\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 @reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw15082uz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
