\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore dlr fluctuations normal - trade minister. \b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2000\par 04:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 5 (Reuters) - Singapore's trade and industry minister George Yeo said on Wednesday recent fluctuations in the Singapore dollar were due to "normal volatility". \par \par \uc2  "It's just normal volatility," he said, declining further comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Yeo was speaking to reporters at the sidelines of a conference in Singapore. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers had said there were rumours in the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, buying the U.S. dollar around the S$1.65 level to slow the Singapore dollar's recent rise. \par \par \uc2  A MAS official on Tuesday declined comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rumours. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  traditionally says it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to smoothe sharp fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Singapore dollar's upside could be limited now as players would remain wary of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but most expect it to appreciate in the months ahead as inflation picks up in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  At 0320 GMT, the Singapore unit was trading at S$1.6550/60 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  ((Singapore newsroom (65) 8703080 fax: (65) 7768112 singapore.newsroom@reuters.comm)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1507yp1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal25