\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Lose lustre as stocks take a hit. \b0\par\par\uc2 975 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2000\par 03:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 5 (Reuters) - Sharp falls across key \par \par \uc2  regional stock markets took the shine off most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Wednesday, with the recently high-flying baht\tab     taking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par one of the heaviest hits.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Heavy overnight losses on Wall Street knocked the wind out\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of key Asian stock markets, but analysts reckoned it provided\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par an excuse to take profits after recent sharp gains and did not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par represent a significant shift in sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said the appreciative trend in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remained.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A more than three percent fall in Japanese stocks also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par played its part in pressuring the yen\tab    .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Tokyo said upside for dollar/yen was limited\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par though as solid bids by some Japanese investors were detected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par below 103.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     New Zealand markets re-opened for their first day of trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after their extended new year break.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the economic indicator front, Taiwan was due to release\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closely watched December consumer price index (CPI) data at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0300 GMT while the Philippines published inflation data for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par December 1999 at 0100 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht slid as major European and U.S. names bought the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar to settle mismatched forward contracts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Importers were in the market to take advantage of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht's recent gains, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The Dow's fall overnight will also ease the upward\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure on the baht because funds might slow down investments\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the stock market for now while monitoring the situation,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said a Singapore-based dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "And technically, the baht has been heavily overbought\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lately. So, some selling is to be expected," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar lost some ground in line with a heavy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par drop on the Straits Time share index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers cited rumours that the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the market on Tuesday, buying U.S. dollars around the 1.65\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level to slow the Sing dollar's recent rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  does not comment on\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but has said that it \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par smooth sharp moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the Sing dollar's upside could be limited for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par now as players would remain wary of the MAS, but most expect it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to rise in the months ahead as inflation picks up in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A more than four percent fall in domestic stocks weighed on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the won, forcing it to open at around 1,125 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It had closed at 1,122 the previous day on the back of fat\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains in the KOSPI -- its highest levels in almost two years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said they expected it to trade in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,120-1,130 range for the rest of the day partly due to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sell-off in stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But they said the bullish mood in equities remained intact\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the KOSPI's drop was being driven by profit-taking, as with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the rest of the region.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar bucked the regional uptrend and held on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to its firmer tone.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It was bid at around 30.50 per dollar early, above its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close of T$30.6 the previous day and way above its recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par string of 25-month highs around the T$31.39 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore dealers said fundamentals remained strong for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan and that an overnight glitch on Wall Street would not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par have any lasting impact.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     One dealer with a European bank said it was seen heading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par towards 30.00 per dollar near-term but that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would probably enter the market to slow its rise at around the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 30.20 mark.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso lost ground in line with other regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and especially the baht, which it tends to track as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par both markets compete in similar export markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But it was still the right side of 40 per dollar after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closing at a 17-week high of 39.77 on the back of capital\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows from foreign funds the previous day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said dollar/peso was likely to firm further if\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/baht headed back towards the 38 per dollar level and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that it would also take its cue from the mood in stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CPI rose 4.3 percent in the year to December 1999 against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par an annual 3.9 percent rise in November. Economists polled by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters had expected the figure to come in at 4.35 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah lost around two percent in thin early trade as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players continued to monitor the financial health of Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia, the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A critical state audit of the bank last week suggested its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par finances were so problematic it might need to be recapitalised.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     All eyes were on domestic stocks after they hit six-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par highs the previous day, with players waiting to see the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reaction to Wall Street's falls.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0155 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     102.93\tab  102.90\tab    -0.03\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6568\tab  1.6510\tab    -0.35\par  Taiwan dlr     30.53\tab   30.57\tab    +0.13\par  Korean won   1126.60\tab 1121.00\tab    -0.50\par  Baht\tab      37.22\tab   36.80\tab    -1.13\par  Peso\tab      39.95\tab   39.74\tab    -0.53\par  Rupiah\tab  7180.00\tab 7030.00\tab    -2.09\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7998\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     102.93\tab  102.21\tab    -0.70\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6568\tab  1.6640\tab    +0.43\par  Taiwan dlr     30.53\tab   31.38\tab    +2.78\par  Korean won   1126.60\tab 1135.00\tab    +0.75\par  Baht\tab      37.22\tab   37.45\tab    +0.62\par  Peso\tab      39.95\tab   40.20\tab    +0.63\par  Rupiah\tab  7180.00\tab 6975.00\tab    -2.86\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7997\tab    -0.00\par \tab   ((Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Desk (65) 870-3087\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par email:asia.\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 @reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1507w9r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
