\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Weaker Late On Stock Market Sell-Off \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2000\par 10:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar is weaker against the U.S. dollar late Wednesday following a hefty drop in stock prices, dealers say. \par \par \uc2  At about 0850 GMT (3:50 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6567, up from S$1.6535 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Straits Times Industrial Index plummeted more than 5.5% Wednesday, taking its lead from a 3.2% decline in the Dow Jones Industrial Average the previous day. \par \par \uc2  The equity market sell-off reversed the Singapore dollar's strong upward trend, which saw it hit an intraday high of S$1.6465 against the U.S. dollar Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But dealers say the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reversal is temporary since the stock market correction has run it's course and heavy capital flows are seen entering Asia in the new year. \par \par \uc2  An analyst at a U.K. bank said strong economic fundamentals as well as renewed stock market strength will put upward pressure on the Singapore dollar in the near term. \par \par \uc2  He said, however, that fears of a U.S. dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  will support the U.S. dollar at S$1.6500. \par \par \uc2  This week, he said the U.S. dollar will trade between S$1.6500 and S$1.6600. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 0.125%, down from 0.250% late Tuesday, while the three-month rate was offered unchanged at 2.4375%. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807; anita.jain@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw15000p1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
