\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mood bullish, Taiwan dlr jumps. \b0\par\par\uc2 986 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2000\par 02:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 4 (Reuters) - The mood was bullish for Asian \par \par \uc2  regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday as some domestic markets \par \par \uc2  re-opened for their first day of trade this year. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Singapore said the focus was on regional stock \par \par \uc2  markets after key indices that had resumed trade the previous \par \par \uc2  day hit record highs. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar\tab     jumped more than one percent as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign funds soaked up stocks on that market's first trading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Financial markets also re-opened in Japan, South Korea, and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand, with Indonesian stocks also resuming activity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Only New Zealand's markets were still closed and were set\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to re-start on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen\tab     was steady despite wariness of possible Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Japan yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Dealers in Tokyo said fund\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par repatriation by local banks, now that Y2K had been a non-event,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could lend it support.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippines expected November export numbers at 0100\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT while Thailand was slated to release consumer price and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wholesale price data at 0400 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fresh momentum in domestic stocks helped push the Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar above T$31 per dollar during its first day of domestic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade after the new year break, representing new 25-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par highs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said they were aware of the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hand anywhere above the T$31\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level for the local unit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders in Taipei said the Taiwan dollar had also drawn\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inspiration from bullishness in the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Speculative offshore dollar sales pushed the won above its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1999 high of 1,125.0, sparking moves by the monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities to temper its rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said the authorities had entered\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the local market to buy dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders in Singapore said the won's direction would depend\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the appetite for domestic stocks -- Asia's top performer in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1999 -- as trade got underway.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     One analyst from a European bank said the Bank of Korea was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to condone a stronger won as the year progressed,\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  less frequently in order to keep inflation at bay.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht shed some of Monday's steep gains, which were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par driven by offshore players unwinding long dollar positions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after a smooth crossover to the new year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the baht should appreciate in the medium-term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But some consolidation was expected this week as the dollar was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par already deep in oversold territory with a reading of 13.65 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 14-day relative strength index (RSI).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The onshore market resumed activity on Tuesday and players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were awaiting the release of consumer and wholesale price data\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at 0400 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market will also watch closely the Bank of Thailand's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par plan to revamp its monetary policy. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recently\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par submitted a draft to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The draft seeks greater independence in pursuing an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation-targetted monetary policy. It is expected to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par publicise details of the plan on January 20-21.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It will take months for the draft to be passed into law.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Capital inflows into the stock market jolted the Singapore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar higher against the U.S. dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some analysts expected the blue-chip Straits Times Index\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    to head toward 2,700 by late January from around 2,500\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par now.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said although the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could rise to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.50-1.60 level by the end of this year, the government is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to be cautious and unwilling to allow to rapid an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appreciation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO (PHP=)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso edged up against the dollar as players continued\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to unwind long dollar positions they kept from late last year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par due to concerns over potential millennium computer glitches.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Sentiment was also boosted by robust trade data released by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the National Statistics Office (NSO) on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Philippine exports in November reached $3.073 billion, up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 18.8 percent from a year ago. In January-November, exports\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reached $32.089 billion, up 19 percent from $26.973 billion in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the same period in 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But dealers reckoned any rise in the peso would be gradual\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as foreign funds were likely to concentrate on big stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets such as those in Singapore, Hong Kong and South Korea\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was a shade weaker, with Singapore dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par saying trade was thin as investors continued to monitor\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par political and economic developments in Indonesia in the new\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Concerns about the precarious financial situation of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weighed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Several analysts were upbeat on the rupiah's prospects on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the basis that it has been undervalued and that economic growth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this year should underpin its firmer tone.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     One analyst from a U.S. bank said dollar/rupiah was likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to trade between 6,850 and 7,300 in the next couple of weeks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and slip to around 6,500 later in the year.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0136 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     101.53\tab  101.77\tab    +0.24\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6572\tab  1.6580\tab    +0.05\par  Taiwan dlr     30.96\tab   31.33\tab    +1.20\par  Korean won   1126.00\tab 1127.00\tab    +0.09\par  Baht\tab      36.90\tab   36.78\tab    -0.33\par  Peso\tab      39.81\tab   39.97\tab    +0.40\par  Rupiah\tab  7075.00\tab 7050.00\tab    -0.35\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     101.53\tab  102.21\tab    +0.67\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6572\tab  1.6640\tab    +0.41\par  Taiwan dlr     30.96\tab   31.38\tab    +1.36\par  Korean won   1126.00\tab 1135.00\tab    +0.80\par  Baht\tab      36.90\tab   37.45\tab    +1.49\par  Peso\tab      39.81\tab   40.20\tab    +0.98\par  Rupiah\tab  7075.00\tab 6975.00\ta