\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Open Mixed But Mood Remains Bullish \b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2000\par 01:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mixed against the U.S. dollar as Asian trading hours begin Tuesday, but after a strong start to the year Monday, sentiment toward regional markets remains robustly bullish. \par \par \uc2  "We're seeing a bit of (dollar) selling. It looks like people are changing dollars into local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to invest locally," said a Singapore broker, reporting U.S. dollar offers from investment banks in early dealing. \par \par \uc2  Despite fears of possible U.S. dollar-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , following yet another record performance Monday from the Singapore stock market, dealers in the overnight market in New York did not balk at selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down against the Singapore dollar, breaking below the perceived S$1.6590 danger level to hit a low of S$1.6558. \par \par \uc2  At 0015 GMT (7:15 p.m. Monday EST), the U.S. dollar was quoted against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at S$1.6569, down from S$1.6600 late in Asia the previous day. \par \par \uc2  After the Thai baht strengthened in offshore trading Monday, hitting its highest level since August 1999 while the Bangkok market was closed for a holiday, dealers expect the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken a touch Tuesday with the return of Thai corporate dollar demand when local markets reopen. \par \par \uc2  Against the baht, the U.S. dollar was quoted at THB36.9500, up from THB36.8500 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah, the U.S. dollar was at IDR7,055, down slightly from IDR7,070 late the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Trading on the Philippine Dealing System is due to open at 0100 GMT. At the close of trading Monday, the U.S. dollar was at 39.980 pesos. \par \par \uc2  In North Asia, trading in the won is set to restart at 0030 GMT after the New Year break amid strongly bullish sentiment toward Korean markets. At the previous close Thursday, the dollar was quoted against the won at KRW1,138.00. \par \par \uc2  Domestic dealing in Taipei is scheduled to reopen at 0100 GMT. At the end of Thursday's session the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted against the New Taiwan dollar at NT$31.395. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw14001am\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
