\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Steady amid settlement jitters. \b0\par\par\uc2 834 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 1999\par 04:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Dec 28 (Reuters) - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  kept within narrow ranges as trade wound down further on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday, with some concern over settlement dampening interest \par \par \uc2  further. \par \par \uc2      Most markets in Asia will be closed on December 31 and \par \par \uc2  some, like South Korea and the Philippines, are shut on \par \par \uc2  Thursday to give banks and brokerages enough time to prepare \par \par \uc2  for the millenium change. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said trade was likely to grind to a virtual halt by \par \par \uc2  Wednesday as most players would want to avoid the risk of \par \par \uc2  settling after the new year begins. \par \par \uc2      The dollar was struggling to build a rally despite pockets \par \par \uc2  of customer demand and rumours of Bank of Japan rate checking. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It soon subsided from a high of 102.70 yen\tab    , reached\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on a couple of buy orders in a very illiquid market, and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers said exporters offers in the 102.70/103.00 region had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par formed a solid ceiling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON\tab     -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won was slightly lower as the state-run Korea\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Development Bank kept up its dollar purchases and importers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bought dollars in a thin market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Seoul traders said players were reluctant to take positions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par given the tussle between Korean authorities trying to stop the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par won strengthening, and expectations that foreign appetite for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korean stocks would push it through 1,110 in Q1 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government said it would spend more than a third of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2000 budget in the first quarter of the year to bolster job\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par creation programmes and public works spending.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was little changed in slow trade, with local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate dollar demand seen limiting its upside. But dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said the government could take advantage of a thin market to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par try and push the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Jakarta \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market will be closed from December 31 to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par January 2 when there is no interbank clearing and will reopen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht remained in a tight range as commercial demand\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dwindled ahead of the year end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday assured the market that it has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reserved 400 billion baht of banknotes which should be more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than enough to cope with withdrawals triggered by Y2K worries.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It said Thais had drawn about 146 billion baht ($3.87\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion) from bank deposit accounts during December 1-24 and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the figure should rise to 239 billion baht by the end of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par December.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This means the Bank of Thailand might not have to drain\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht liquidity from the offshore market for domestic use as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par feared by some market participants.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso drifted lower in a thin year-end market, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers reckoned there was more room for the upside after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par turn of the year due to inflows and an improved economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outlook.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The country's volume of production index was up 8.7 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year-on-year in October. This is the third consecutive month of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positive growth in the manufacturing sector.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar extended its gains after hitting a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 25-month closing high the previous day, with dealers expecting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it to challenge the T$31.5 per dollar level soon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taipei dealers said there had been no sign of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the previous day when foreign fund stock buying\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gave the local unit a boost.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollar sales by exporters ahead of year-end gave the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more upward momentum, but its rise was expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to be capped by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and some U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-covering.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar was little changed as banks limited\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par activity to a bare minimum ahead of the year-end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Speculative plays were not expected to emerge until Y2K\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fears had dissipated and trading books had re-opened for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par new year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some analysts expect the Sing dollar to appreciate to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1.65 at the beginning of next year on the back of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par further signs of economic growth and a buoyant stock market.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0310 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     102.30\tab  102.58\tab    +0.27\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6676\tab  1.6682\tab    +0.04\par  Taiwan dlr     31.47\tab   31.53\tab    +0.19\par  Korean won   1135.30\tab 1133.50\tab    -0.16\par  Baht\tab      37.62\tab   37.70\tab    +0.21\par  Peso\tab      40.28\tab   40.21\tab    -0.17\par  Rupiah\tab  6985.00\tab 6990.00\tab    +0.07\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.8000\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     102.30\tab  113.20\tab   +10.65\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6676\tab  1.6495\tab    -1.09\par  Taiwan dlr     31.47\tab   32.17\tab    +2.22\par  Korean won   1135.30\tab 1200.00\tab    +5.70\par  Baht\tab      37.62\tab   36.20\tab    -3.77\par  Peso\tab      40.28\tab   38.75\tab    -3.80\par  Rupiah\tab  6985.00\tab 