\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Open A Touch Stronger; Seen Range-Bound \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 1999\par 01:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are a touch stronger against the U.S. dollar as local trading hours begin Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Activity is subdued, however, and dealers see the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remaining range-bound through Asian trading hours. \par \par \uc2  Already winding down ahead of the end of the year, dealing in regional markets is expected to slow further with the beginning of Ramadan this week. \par \par \uc2  The strength of the Singapore stock market is likely to lend support to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, traders said. But fear of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to suppress the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise is likely to deter any U.S. dollar-selling below S$1.6750, they added. \par \par \uc2  At 0015 GMT (7:15 p.m. Tuesday EST), the U.S. dollar was quoted against the Singapore dollar at S$1.6765, compared with S$1.6791 late in Asia the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the U.S. dollar was quoted at THB38.6750, down from THB38.7600 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah, the U.S. dollar was at IDR7,210, a touch lower than IDR7,215 late the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Trading on the Philippine Dealing System is due to open at 0100 GMT. At the close of trading Tuesday, the U.S. dollar was at PHP40.730. \par \par \uc2  In North Asia, trading in the won is set to start at 0030 GMT. \par \par \uc2  After the won hit a two-year high Tuesday, with the dollar dropping to an intraday low of 1,132.50 won, most market participants expect the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall further against the won, although its descent may be interrupted by official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At Tuesday's close, the dollar was trading at KRW1,139.50. \par \par \uc2  Domestic dealing in Taipei is scheduled to begin at 0100 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar is expected to continue to grind higher against \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after it too set a new two-year high Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At the end of Tuesday's session, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted against the New Taiwan dollar at NT$31.600. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvc808cg6\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Singapore near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs 